\p \v 1 \rb In the year|בִּשְׁנַת־\rb* \rb that King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Uzziah|עֻזִּיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb died,|מוֹת֙\rb* \rb I saw|וָאֶרְאֶ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֛י\rb* \rb seated|יֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb a throne,|כִּסֵּ֖א\rb* \rb high|רָ֣ם\rb* \rb and exalted;|וְנִשָּׂ֑א\rb* \rb and the train of His robe|וְשׁוּלָ֖יו\rb*\f + \fr 6:1 \ft Or \fqa the hem of His robe\f* \rb filled|מְלֵאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple.|הַהֵיכָֽל׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Above|מִמַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb Him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb stood|עֹמְדִ֤ים׀\rb* \rb seraphim,|שְׂרָפִ֨ים\rb* \rb each|לְאֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb having six|שֵׁ֧שׁ\rb* \rb wings:|כְּנָפַ֛יִם\rb* \rb With two wings|בִּשְׁתַּ֣יִם׀\rb* \rb they covered|יְכַסֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb their faces,|פָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb with two|וּבִשְׁתַּ֛יִם\rb* \rb they covered|יְכַסֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb their feet,|רַגְלָ֖יו\rb* \rb and with two|וּבִשְׁתַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb they were flying.|יְעוֹפֵֽף׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And they|זֶ֤ה\rb* \rb were calling out|וְקָרָ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one another:|זֶה֙\rb*\rb |וְאָמַ֔ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Holy,|קָד֧וֹשׁ׀\rb* \rb holy,|קָד֛וֹשׁ\rb* \rb holy|קָד֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb is the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts;|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb is full|מְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb of His glory.”|כְּבוֹדֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb At the sound|מִקּ֖וֹל\rb* \rb of their voices|הַקּוֹרֵ֑א\rb* \rb the doorposts|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and thresholds|הַסִּפִּ֔ים\rb* \rb shook,|וַיָּנֻ֙עוּ֙\rb* \rb and the temple|וְהַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb was filled|יִמָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb with smoke.|עָשָֽׁן׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then I said:|וָאֹמַ֞ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Woe|אֽוֹי־\rb* \rb is me,|לִ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִֽי־\rb* \rb I am ruined,|נִדְמֵ֗יתִי\rb*
\q1 \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אָנֹ֔כִי\rb* \rb am a man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb of unclean|טְמֵֽא־\rb* \rb lips|שְׂפָתַ֙יִם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb dwelling|יוֹשֵׁ֑ב\rb* \rb among|וּבְתוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb a people|עַם־\rb* \rb of unclean|טְמֵ֣א\rb* \rb lips;|שְׂפָתַ֔יִם\rb*\rb |אָנֹכִ֖י\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינָֽי׃\rb* \rb have seen|רָא֥וּ\rb* \rb the King,|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.”|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Then one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the seraphim|הַשְּׂרָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb flew|וַיָּ֣עָף\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb and in his hand|וּבְיָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb was a glowing coal|רִצְפָּ֑ה\rb* \rb that he had taken|לָקַ֖ח\rb* \rb with tongs|בְּמֶ֨לְקַחַ֔יִם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb the altar.|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb* \v 7 \rb And with it he touched|וַיַּגַּ֣ע\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb my mouth|פִּ֔י\rb* \rb and said:|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Now that|הִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb this|זֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb has touched|נָגַ֥ע\rb* \rb your lips,|שְׂפָתֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb your iniquity|עֲוֺנֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb is removed|וְסָ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and your sin|וְחַטָּאתְךָ֖\rb* \rb is atoned for.”|תְּכֻפָּֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then I heard|וָאֶשְׁמַ֞ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the voice|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָי֙\rb* \rb saying:|אֹמֵ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Whom|מִ֥י\rb* \rb shall I send?|אֶשְׁלַ֖ח\rb*
\q2 \rb Who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb will go|יֵֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb for Us?”|לָ֑נוּ\rb*
\p \rb And I said:|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Here am I.|הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb Send me!”|שְׁלָחֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb And He replied:|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Go|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֖\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb people,|לָעָ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb ‘Be ever hearing,|שִׁמְע֤וּ\rb*\rb |שָׁמ֙וֹעַ֙\rb* \rb but never|וְאַל־\rb* \rb understanding;|תָּבִ֔ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb be ever seeing,|וּרְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |רָא֖וֹ\rb* \rb but never|וְאַל־\rb* \rb perceiving.’|תֵּדָֽעוּ׃\rb*\f + \fr 6:9 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa ‘You shall be ever hearing, but never understanding; you shall be ever seeing, but never perceiving.’\ft Cited in \ref Matthew 13:14|MAT 13:14\ref*, Mark 4:12, Luke 8:10, and Acts 28:26\f*
\q1 \v 10 \rb Make the hearts|לֵב־\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb calloused;|הַשְׁמֵן֙\rb*
\q2 \rb deafen|הַכְבֵּ֖ד\rb* \rb their ears|וְאָזְנָ֥יו\rb* \rb and close|הָשַׁ֑ע\rb* \rb their eyes.|וְעֵינָ֣יו\rb*
\q1 \rb Otherwise|פֶּן־\rb* \rb they might see|יִרְאֶ֨ה\rb* \rb with their eyes,|בְעֵינָ֜יו\rb*
\q2 \rb hear|יִשְׁמָ֗ע\rb* \rb with their ears,|וּבְאָזְנָ֣יו\rb*
\q2 \rb understand|יָבִ֛ין\rb* \rb with their hearts,|וּלְבָב֥וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb and turn|וָשָׁ֖ב\rb* \rb and be healed.|וְרָ֥פָא\rb*\f + \fr 6:10 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa For this people’s heart has grown callous; they hardly hear with their ears, and they have closed their eyes. Otherwise they might see with their eyes, hear with their ears, understand with their hearts, and turn, and I would heal them.\ft Cited in \ref Matthew 13:15|MAT 13:15\ref*, Mark 4:12, John 12:40, and Acts 28:27\f*”
\p \v 11 \rb Then I asked:|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “How long,|עַד־\rb*\rb |מָתַ֖י\rb* \rb O Lord?”|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb*
\p \rb And He replied:|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb lie ruined|שָׁא֨וּ\rb*
\q1 \rb and without|מֵאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb inhabitant,|יוֹשֵׁ֗ב\rb*
\q1 \rb until the houses|וּבָתִּים֙\rb* \rb are left unoccupied|מֵאֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |אָדָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and the land|וְהָאֲדָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb is desolate|תִּשָּׁאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb and ravaged,|שְׁמָמָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb until the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has driven men|הָאָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb far away|וְרִחַ֥ק\rb*
\q2 \rb and the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb is utterly|וְרַבָּ֥ה\rb* \rb forsaken.|הָעֲזוּבָ֖ה\rb*\rb |בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb And though|וְע֥וֹד\rb* \rb a tenth remains|עֲשִׂ֣רִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb in the land,|בָּהּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb it will be|וְהָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb burned|לְבָעֵ֑ר\rb* \rb again.|וְשָׁ֖בָה\rb*
\q1 \rb As the terebinth|כָּאֵלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and oak|וְכָאַלּ֗וֹן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb leave stumps|מַצֶּ֣בֶת\rb* \rb when felled,|בְּשַׁלֶּ֙כֶת֙\rb*
\q2 \rb so the holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb seed|זֶ֥רַע\rb* \rb will be a stump in the land.”|מַצַּבְתָּֽהּ׃פ\rb*
\c 7
\s1 A Message to Ahaz
\p \v 1 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb in the days that|בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָ֠חָז\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jotham,|יוֹתָ֨ם\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Uzziah,|עֻזִּיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb was king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb Rezin|רְצִ֣ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲ֠רָם\rb*\f + \fr 7:1 \ft That is, Syria\f* \rb marched up|עָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb to wage war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb against|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb Jerusalem.|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb He was accompanied by Pekah|וּפֶ֨קַח\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Remaliah|רְמַלְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb but he could|יָכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb overpower|לְהִלָּחֵ֥ם\rb* \rb the city.|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb When it was reported|וַיֻּגַּ֗ד\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֤ית\rb* \rb of David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb that Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb was in league with|נָ֥חָֽה\rb* \rb Ephraim,|אֶפְרָ֑יִם\rb*\f + \fr 7:2 \ft Or \fqa had set up camp in Ephraim\ft , that is, the northern kingdom of Israel\f* \rb the hearts|לְבָבוֹ֙\rb* \rb of Ahaz|וּלְבַ֣ב\rb* \rb and his people|עַמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb trembled|וַיָּ֤נַע\rb* \rb like trees|עֲצֵי־\rb* \rb in the forest|יַ֖עַר\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵי־\rb* \rb shaken|כְּנ֥וֹעַ\rb* \rb by the wind.|רֽוּחַ׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Isaiah,|יְשַׁעְיָהוּ֒\rb* \rb “Go out|צֵא־\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb* \rb with your son|בְּנֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |וּשְׁאָ֖ר\rb* \rb Shear-jashub|יָשׁ֣וּב\rb*\f + \fr 7:3 \fqa Shear-jashub \ft means \fqa a remnant shall return\ft .\f* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֔ז\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the end|קְצֵ֗ה\rb* \rb of the aqueduct|תְּעָלַת֙\rb* \rb that feeds the upper|הָעֶלְיוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb pool,|הַבְּרֵכָ֣ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the road|מְסִלַּ֖ת\rb* \rb to the Launderer’s|כוֹבֵֽס׃\rb* \rb Field,|שְׂדֵ֥ה\rb* \v 4 \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to him:|אֵ֠לָיו\rb* \rb Calm down|הִשָּׁמֵ֨ר\rb* \rb and be quiet.|וְהַשְׁקֵ֜ט\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֗א\rb* \rb or disheartened|וּלְבָבְךָ֙\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb*\rb |יֵרַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb over these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb two|מִשְּׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb smoldering|הָעֲשֵׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb stubs|זַנְב֧וֹת\rb* \rb of firewood—|הָאוּדִ֛ים\rb* \rb over the fierce|בָּחֳרִי־\rb* \rb anger|אַ֛ף\rb* \rb of Rezin|רְצִ֥ין\rb* \rb and Aram|וַאֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb and of the son|וּבֶן־\rb* \rb of Remaliah.|רְמַלְיָֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 5 \rb For|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Aram,|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb along with Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֥יִם\rb* \rb and the son|וּבֶן־\rb* \rb of Remaliah,|רְמַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb has plotted|יָעַ֥ץ\rb* \rb your ruin,|רָעָ֑ה\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 6 \rb ‘Let us invade|נַעֲלֶ֤ה\rb* \rb Judah,|בִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb terrorize it,|וּנְקִיצֶ֔נָּה\rb* \rb and divide it|וְנַבְקִעֶ֖נָּה\rb*\f + \fr 7:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa split it open\f* \rb among ourselves.|אֵלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb Then we can install|מֶ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Tabeal|טָֽבְאַֽל׃ס\rb* \rb over it|בְּתוֹכָ֔הּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb as king.’|וְנַמְלִ֥יךְ\rb* \v 7 \rb But this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֖ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb ‘It will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb arise;|תָק֖וּם\rb*
\q2 \rb it will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb happen.|תִֽהְיֶֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֤אשׁ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb is Damascus,|דַּמֶּ֔שֶׂק\rb*
\q2 \rb and the head|וְרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַּמֶּ֖שֶׂק\rb* \rb is Rezin.|רְצִ֑ין\rb*
\q1 \rb Within|וּבְע֗וֹד\rb* \rb sixty-five|שִׁשִּׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will be shattered|יֵחַ֥ת\rb* \rb as a people.|מֵעָֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb The head|וְרֹ֤אשׁ\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb is Samaria,|שֹׁמְר֔וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and the head|וְרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb is the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Remaliah.|רְמַלְיָ֑הוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb If|אִ֚ם\rb* \rb you do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb stand firm in your faith,|תַאֲמִ֔ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb then|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb stand at all.’”|תֵאָמֵֽנוּ׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Sign of Immanuel
\r \ref Matthew 1:18–25|MAT 1:18-25\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb Again|וַיּ֣וֹסֶף\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb spoke|דַּבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahaz,|אָחָ֖ז\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 11 \rb “Ask|שְׁאַל־\rb* \rb for|לְךָ֣\rb* \rb a sign|א֔וֹת\rb* \rb from|מֵעִ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb whether from the depths|הַעְמֵ֣ק\rb* \rb of Sheol|שְׁאָ֔לָה\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb the heights|הַגְבֵּ֥הַּ\rb* \rb of heaven.”|לְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But Ahaz|אָחָ֑ז\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “I will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb ask;|אֶשְׁאַ֥ל\rb* \rb I will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb test|אֲנַסֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Then Isaiah said,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Hear|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb* \rb now,|נָ֖א\rb* \rb O house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of David!|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb Is it not enough|הַמְעַ֤ט\rb*\rb |מִכֶּם֙\rb* \rb to try the patience|הַלְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of men?|אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Will you try the patience|תַלְא֖וּ\rb* \rb of my God|אֱלֹהָֽי׃\rb* \rb as well?|גַּ֥ם\rb* \v 14 \rb Therefore|לָ֠כֵן\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb Himself|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb will give|יִתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a sign:|א֑וֹת\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb the virgin|הָעַלְמָ֗ה\rb*\f + \fr 7:14 \ft Or \fqa young woman\f* \rb will be with child|הָרָה֙\rb* \rb and give birth|וְיֹלֶ֣דֶת\rb* \rb to a son,|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb and will call|וְקָרָ֥את\rb* \rb Him|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |עִמָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb Immanuel.|אֵֽל׃\rb*\f + \fr 7:14 \fqa Immanuel \ft means \fqa God with us\ft ; literally \fqa and she will call His name Immanuel\ft ; DSS \fqa and His name will be called Immanuel \ft or \fqa and He will call His name Immanuel\ft ; LXX \fqa and you will call His name Immanuel\ft ; cited in \ref Matthew 1:23|MAT 1:23\ref*.\f* \v 15 \rb By the time He knows enough|לְדַעְתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb to reject|מָא֥וֹס\rb* \rb evil|בָּרָ֖ע\rb* \rb and choose|וּבָח֥וֹר\rb* \rb good,|בַּטּֽוֹב׃\rb* \rb He will be eating|יֹאכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb curds|חֶמְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb and honey.|וּדְבַ֖שׁ\rb* \v 16 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb before|בְּטֶ֨רֶם\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֛עַר\rb* \rb knows enough|יֵדַ֥ע\rb* \rb to reject|מָאֹ֥ס\rb* \rb evil|בָּרָ֖ע\rb* \rb and choose|וּבָחֹ֣ר\rb* \rb good,|בַּטּ֑וֹב\rb* \rb the land|הָאֲדָמָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of the two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb dread|קָ֔ץ\rb*\rb |מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb will be laid waste.|תֵּעָזֵ֤ב\rb*
