\s1 Darkness and Light
\p \v 19 \rb When|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb men tell|יֹאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb you|אֲלֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb to consult|דִּרְשׁ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb mediums|הָאֹבוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and spiritists|הַיִּדְּעֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who whisper|הַֽמְצַפְצְפִ֖ים\rb* \rb and mutter,|וְהַמַּהְגִּ֑ים\rb* \rb shouldn’t|הֲלוֹא־\rb* \rb a people|עַם֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb consult|יִדְרֹ֔שׁ\rb* \rb their God instead?|אֱלֹהָ֣יו\rb* \rb Why consult the dead|הַמֵּתִֽים׃\rb* \rb on behalf of|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb the living?|הַחַיִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \v 20 \rb To the law|לְתוֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb and to the testimony!|וְלִתְעוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb they do not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb speak|יֹֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb according to this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb word,|כַּדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb they have no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb light of dawn.|שָֽׁחַר׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb They will roam the land,|וְעָ֥בַר\rb* \rb dejected|נִקְשֶׁ֣ה\rb* \rb and hungry.|וְרָעֵ֑ב\rb*\rb |וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb When|כִֽי־\rb* \rb they are famished,|יִרְעַ֜ב\rb* \rb they will become enraged;|וְהִתְקַצַּ֗ף\rb* \rb and looking|וּפָנָ֥ה\rb* \rb upward,|לְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb they will curse|וְקִלֵּ֧ל\rb* \rb their king|בְּמַלְכּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb and their God.|וּבֵאלֹהָ֖יו\rb* \v 22 \rb Then they will look|יַבִּ֑יט\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the earth|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb and see|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb only distress|צָרָ֤ה\rb* \rb and darkness|וַחֲשֵׁכָה֙\rb* \rb and the gloom|מְע֣וּף\rb* \rb of anguish.|צוּקָ֔ה\rb* \rb And they will be driven|מְנֻדָּֽח׃\rb* \rb into utter darkness.|וַאֲפֵלָ֖ה\rb*
\c 9
\s1 Unto Us a Child Is Born
