\q1 \rb I will end|וְהִשְׁבַּתִּי֙\rb* \rb the haughtiness|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the arrogant|זֵדִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and lay low|אַשְׁפִּֽיל׃\rb* \rb the pride|וְגַאֲוַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the ruthless.|עָרִיצִ֖ים\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb I will make man|אֱנ֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb scarcer|אוֹקִ֥יר\rb* \rb than pure gold,|מִפָּ֑ז\rb*
\q2 \rb and mankind|וְאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb rarer than the gold|מִכֶּ֥תֶם\rb* \rb of Ophir.|אוֹפִֽיר׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֙\rb* \rb I will make the heavens|שָׁמַ֣יִם\rb* \rb tremble,|אַרְגִּ֔יז\rb*
\q2 \rb and the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb will be shaken|וְתִרְעַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb from its place|מִמְּקוֹמָ֑הּ\rb*
\q1 \rb at the wrath|בְּעֶבְרַת֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb on the day|וּבְי֖וֹם\rb* \rb of His burning anger.|חֲר֥וֹן\rb*\rb |אַפּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb |וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb Like a hunted|מֻדָּ֔ח\rb* \rb gazelle,|כִּצְבִ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb like a sheep|וּכְצֹ֖אן\rb* \rb without|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb a shepherd,|מְקַבֵּ֑ץ\rb*
\q1 \rb each|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb will return|יִפְנ֔וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own people,|עַמּוֹ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb each|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb will flee|יָנֽוּסוּ׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his native land.|אַרְצ֖וֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb Whoever|כָּל־\rb* \rb is caught|הַנִּמְצָ֖א\rb* \rb will be stabbed,|יִדָּקֵ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and whoever|וְכָל־\rb* \rb is captured|הַנִּסְפֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb will die|יִפּ֥וֹל\rb* \rb by the sword.|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb Their infants|וְעֹלְלֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb will be dashed to pieces|יְרֻטְּשׁ֖וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb before their eyes,|לְעֵֽינֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*
\q1 \rb their houses|בָּֽתֵּיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb will be looted,|יִשַּׁ֙סּוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and their wives|וּנְשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will be ravished.|תִּשָּׁגַלְנָה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֛י\rb* \rb I will stir up|מֵעִ֥יר\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the Medes,|מָדָ֑י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb have no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb regard|יַחְשֹׁ֔בוּ\rb* \rb for silver|כֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb desire|יַחְפְּצוּ־\rb* \rb for gold.|וְזָהָ֖ב\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb Their bows|וּקְשָׁת֖וֹת\rb* \rb will dash young men|נְעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to pieces;|תְּרַטַּ֑שְׁנָה\rb*
\q2 \rb they will have no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb mercy|יְרַחֵ֔מוּ\rb* \rb on the fruit|וּפְרִי־\rb* \rb of the womb;|בֶ֙טֶן֙\rb*
\q2 \rb they will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb look with pity|תָח֥וּס\rb*\rb |עֵינָֽם׃\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the children.|בָּנִ֖ים\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb And Babylon,|בָבֶל֙\rb* \rb the jewel|צְבִ֣י\rb* \rb of the kingdoms,|מַמְלָכ֔וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb the glory|תִּפְאֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb of the pride|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans,|כַּשְׂדִּ֑ים\rb*
\q1 \rb will be|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb overthrown|כְּמַהְפֵּכַ֣ת\rb* \rb by God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb like Sodom|סְדֹ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Gomorrah.|עֲמֹרָֽה׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb She will never|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |לָנֶ֔צַח\rb* \rb be inhabited|תֵשֵׁ֣ב\rb*
\q2 \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb settled|תִשְׁכֹּ֖ן\rb* \rb from|עַד־\rb* \rb generation|דּ֣וֹר\rb* \rb to generation;|וָד֑וֹר\rb*
\q1 \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb nomad|עֲרָבִ֔י\rb* \rb will pitch his tent|יַהֵ֥ל\rb* \rb there,|שָׁם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb shepherd|וְרֹעִ֖ים\rb* \rb will rest his flock|יַרְבִּ֥צוּ\rb* \rb there.|שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 21 \rb But desert creatures|צִיִּ֔ים\rb* \rb will lie down|וְרָבְצוּ־\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and howling creatures|אֹחִ֑ים\rb* \rb will fill|וּמָלְא֥וּ\rb* \rb her houses.|בָתֵּיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\q1 \rb |בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb Ostriches|יַֽעֲנָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 13:21 \ft Literally \fqa Daughters of an ostrich \ft or \fqa Daughters of an owl\f* \rb will dwell|וְשָׁ֤כְנוּ\rb* \rb there,|שָׁם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and wild goats|וּשְׂעִירִ֖ים\rb* \rb will leap about.|יְרַקְּדוּ־\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 22 \rb Hyenas|אִיִּים֙\rb* \rb will howl|וְעָנָ֤ה\rb* \rb in her fortresses|בְּאַלְמנוֹתָ֔יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and jackals|וְתַנִּ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 13:22 \ft Or \fqa serpents \ft or \fqa dragons\f* \rb in her luxurious|עֹ֑נֶג\rb* \rb palaces.|בְּהֵ֣יכְלֵי\rb*
\q1 \rb Babylon’s time|עִתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb is at hand,|וְקָר֤וֹב\rb*\rb |לָבוֹא֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and her days|וְיָמֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be prolonged.|יִמָּשֵֽׁכוּ׃\rb*
\c 14
\s1 Restoration for Israel
\p \v 1 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb will have compassion|יְרַחֵ֨ם\rb* \rb on Jacob;|יַעֲקֹ֗ב\rb* \rb once again|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb He will choose|וּבָחַ֥ר\rb* \rb Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and settle them|וְהִנִּיחָ֖ם\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their own land.|אַדְמָתָ֑ם\rb* \rb The foreigner|הַגֵּר֙\rb* \rb will join them|וְנִלְוָ֤ה\rb* \rb and unite|וְנִסְפְּח֖וּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb with|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Jacob.|יַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb* \v 2 \rb The nations|עַמִּים֮\rb* \rb will escort Israel|וּלְקָח֣וּם\rb* \rb and bring|וֶהֱבִיא֣וּם\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb its homeland.|מְקוֹמָם֒\rb*
\p \rb Then the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb will possess the nations|וְהִֽתְנַחֲל֣וּם\rb* \rb as menservants|לַעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb and maidservants|וְלִשְׁפָח֑וֹת\rb* \rb in|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb land.|אַדְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb They will make|וְהָיוּ֙\rb* \rb captives|שֹׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb of their captors|לְשֹֽׁבֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and rule|וְרָד֖וּ\rb* \rb over their oppressors.|בְּנֹגְשֵׂיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Fall of the King of Babylon
\p \v 3 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb On the day that|בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb gives you rest|הָנִ֤יחַ\rb*\rb |לְךָ֔\rb* \rb from|וּמִן־\rb* \rb your pain|מֵֽעָצְבְּךָ֖\rb* \rb and torment,|וּמֵרָגְזֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and from the hard|הַקָּשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb labor|הָעֲבֹדָ֥ה\rb* \rb into which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you were forced,|עֻבַּד־\rb* \v 4 \rb you will sing|וְנָשָׂ֜אתָ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb song of contempt|הַמָּשָׁ֥ל\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon:|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb*\rb |וְאָמָ֑רְתָּ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb How|אֵ֚יךְ\rb* \rb the oppressor|נֹגֵ֔שׂ\rb* \rb has ceased,|שָׁבַ֣ת\rb*
\q2 \rb and how his fury|מַדְהֵבָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 14:4 \ft DSS, LXX, and Syriac; MT \fqa the golden city\f* \rb has ended!|שָׁבְתָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has broken|שָׁבַ֥ר\rb* \rb the staff|מַטֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb of the wicked,|רְשָׁעִ֑ים\rb*
