\s1 A Blessing upon the Earth
\p \v 16 \rb In that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb like women.|כַּנָּשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb They will tremble|וְחָרַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb with fear|וּפָחַ֗ד\rb* \rb beneath|מִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the uplifted|תְּנוּפַת֙\rb* \rb hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb when He|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb brandishes|מֵנִ֥יף\rb* \rb it|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb against them.|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 17 \rb |וְ֠הָיְתָה\rb* \rb The land|אַדְמַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb will bring terror|לְחָגָּ֔א\rb* \rb to Egypt;|לְמִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb whenever|כֹּל֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Judah is mentioned,|יַזְכִּ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛הּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb Egypt will tremble|יִפְחָ֑ד\rb* \rb over|מִפְּנֵ֗י\rb* \rb what the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb has planned|עֲצַת֙\rb*\rb |יוֹעֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb against it.|עָלָֽיו׃ס\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb In that|הַה֡וּא\rb*\rb |יִהְיוּ֩\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb five|חָמֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb will speak|מְדַבְּרוֹת֙\rb* \rb the language|שְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Canaan|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb* \rb and swear allegiance|וְנִשְׁבָּע֖וֹת\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts.|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb One of them|לְאֶחָֽת׃ס\rb* \rb will be called|יֵאָמֵ֖ר\rb* \rb the City|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of the Sun.|הַהֶ֔רֶס\rb*\f + \fr 19:18 \ft Some MT manuscripts, DSS, and Vulgate; most MT manuscripts \fqa City of Destruction\f*
\p \v 19 \rb In that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb there will be|יִֽהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb an altar|מִזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the center|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt,|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and a pillar|וּמַצֵּבָ֥ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb near|אֵֽצֶל־\rb* \rb her border.|גְּבוּלָ֖הּ\rb* \v 20 \rb It will be|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb a sign|לְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb and a witness|וּלְעֵ֛ד\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt.|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they cry out|יִצְעֲק֤וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb their oppressors,|לֹֽחֲצִ֔ים\rb* \rb He will send|וְיִשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb a savior|מוֹשִׁ֥יעַ\rb* \rb and defender|וָרָ֖ב\rb* \rb to rescue them.|וְהִצִּילָֽם׃\rb* \v 21 \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb will make Himself known|וְנוֹדַ֤ע\rb* \rb to Egypt,|לְמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and on that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will acknowledge|וְיָדְע֥וּ\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb They will worship|וְעָֽבְדוּ֙\rb* \rb with sacrifices|זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb and offerings;|וּמִנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb they will make|וְנָדְרוּ־\rb* \rb vows|נֵ֥דֶר\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and fulfill them.|וְשִׁלֵּֽמוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will strike|וְנָגַ֧ף\rb* \rb Egypt with a plague;|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb He will strike them|נָגֹ֣ף\rb* \rb but heal them.|וְרָפ֑וֹא\rb* \rb They will turn|וְשָׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and He will hear their prayers|וְנֶעְתַּ֥ר\rb* \rb and|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb heal them.|וּרְפָאָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb In that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb there will be|תִּהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb a highway|מְסִלָּ֤ה\rb* \rb from Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb to Assyria.|אַשּׁ֔וּרָה\rb* \rb The Assyrians|אַשּׁ֥וּר\rb* \rb will go|וּבָֽא־\rb* \rb to Egypt,|בְּמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and the Egyptians|וּמִצְרַ֣יִם\rb* \rb to Assyria.|בְּאַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb The Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and Assyrians|אַשּֽׁוּר׃ס\rb* \rb will worship together.|וְעָבְד֥וּ\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb In that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb will join|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb a three-party|שְׁלִ֣ישִׁיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb alliance with Egypt|לְמִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and Assyria—|וּלְאַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb a blessing|בְּרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb upon|בְּקֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 25 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb will bless|בֵּרֲכ֛וֹ\rb* \rb them,|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Blessed be|בָּר֨וּךְ\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb My people,|עַמִּ֜י\rb* \rb Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb My handiwork,|וּמַעֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb*\rb |יָדַי֙\rb* \rb and Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb* \rb My inheritance.”|וְנַחֲלָתִ֖י\rb*
\c 20
\s1 A Sign against Egypt and Cush
\p \v 1 \rb Before the year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb that the chief commander,|תַרְתָּן֙\rb* \rb sent|בִּשְׁלֹ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb by Sargon|סַֽרְג֖וֹן\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria,|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb came|בֹּ֤א\rb* \rb to Ashdod|אַשְׁדּ֔וֹדָה\rb* \rb and attacked|וַיִּלָּ֥חֶם\rb* \rb and captured|וַֽיִּלְכְּדָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb it,|בְּאַשְׁדּ֖וֹד\rb* \v 2 \rb |הַהִ֗יא\rb*\rb |בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb had already spoken|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amoz,|אָמוֹץ֮\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb “Go,|לֵ֗ךְ\rb* \rb remove|וּפִתַּחְתָּ֤\rb* \rb the sackcloth|הַשַּׂק֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb your waist|מָתְנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and|תַחֲלֹ֖ץ\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the sandals|וְנַעַלְךָ֥\rb* \rb from your feet.”|רַגְלֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \rb And Isaiah did|וַיַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb so,|כֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb walking around|הָלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb naked|עָר֥וֹם\rb* \rb and barefoot.|וְיָחֵֽף׃ס\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֥י\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb has gone|הָלַ֛ךְ\rb* \rb naked|עָר֣וֹם\rb* \rb and barefoot|וְיָחֵ֑ף\rb* \rb for three|שָׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִים֙\rb* \rb as a sign|א֣וֹת\rb* \rb and omen|וּמוֹפֵ֔ת\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and Cush,|כּֽוּשׁ׃\rb*\f + \fr 20:3 \ft That is, the upper Nile region; similarly in verses 4 and 5\f* \v 4 \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַ֠שּׁוּר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will lead away|יִנְהַ֣ג\rb* \rb the captives|שְׁבִ֨י\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the exiles|גָּל֥וּת\rb* \rb of Cush,|כּ֛וּשׁ\rb* \rb young|נְעָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and old alike,|וּזְקֵנִ֖ים\rb* \rb naked|עָר֣וֹם\rb* \rb and barefoot,|וְיָחֵ֑ף\rb* \rb with bared|וַחֲשׂוּפַ֥י\rb* \rb buttocks—|שֵׁ֖ת\rb* \rb to Egypt’s|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb shame.|עֶרְוַ֥ת\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Those who made Cush|מִכּוּשׁ֙\rb* \rb their hope|מַבָּטָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb and Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb their boast|תִּפְאַרְתָּֽם׃\rb* \rb will be dismayed|וְחַתּ֖וּ\rb* \rb and ashamed.|וָבֹ֑שׁוּ\rb* \v 6 \rb And on that|הַהוּא֒\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the dwellers|יֹשֵׁ֨ב\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּה֮\rb* \rb coastland|הָאִ֣י\rb* \rb will say,|וְ֠אָמַר\rb* \rb ‘See|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb what has happened|כֹ֣ה\rb* \rb to our source of hope,|מַבָּטֵ֗נוּ\rb* \rb those to whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb we fled|נַ֤סְנוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁם֙\rb* \rb for help|לְעֶזְרָ֔ה\rb* \rb and deliverance|לְהִ֨נָּצֵ֔ל\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria!|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb How then|וְאֵ֖יךְ\rb* \rb can we|אֲנָֽחְנוּ׃ס\rb* \rb escape?’”|נִמָּלֵ֥ט\rb*
\c 21
\s1 Babylon Is Fallen
\r \ref Revelation 18:1–8|REV 18:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb against the Desert|מִדְבַּר־\rb* \rb by the Sea:|יָ֑ם\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Like whirlwinds|כְּסוּפ֤וֹת\rb* \rb sweeping|לַֽחֲלֹ֔ף\rb* \rb through the Negev,|בַּנֶּ֙גֶב֙\rb*
\q2 \rb an invader comes|בָּ֔א\rb* \rb from the desert,|מִמִּדְבָּ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb from a land|מֵאֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of terror.|נוֹרָאָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb A dire|קָשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb vision|חָז֥וּת\rb* \rb is declared|הֻגַּד־\rb* \rb to me:|לִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb “The traitor|הַבּוֹגֵ֤ד׀\rb* \rb still betrays,|בּוֹגֵד֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and the destroyer|וְהַשּׁוֹדֵ֣ד׀\rb* \rb still destroys.|שׁוֹדֵ֔ד\rb*
\q1 \rb Go up,|עֲלִ֤י\rb* \rb O Elam!|עֵילָם֙\rb* \rb Lay siege,|צוּרִ֣י\rb* \rb O Media!|מָדַ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb I will put an end|הִשְׁבַּֽתִּי׃\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her groaning.”|אַנְחָתָ֖ה\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb my body|מָתְנַי֙\rb* \rb is filled|מָלְא֤וּ\rb* \rb with anguish.|חַלְחָלָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb Pain|צִירִ֣ים\rb* \rb grips me,|אֲחָז֔וּנִי\rb* \rb like the pains|כְּצִירֵ֖י\rb* \rb of a woman in labor.|יֽוֹלֵדָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb I am bewildered|נַעֲוֵ֣יתִי\rb* \rb to hear,|מִשְּׁמֹ֔עַ\rb*
\q2 \rb I am dismayed|נִבְהַ֖לְתִּי\rb* \rb to see.|מֵרְאֽוֹת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb My heart|לְבָבִ֔י\rb* \rb falters;|תָּעָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb fear|פַּלָּצ֖וּת\rb* \rb makes me tremble.|בִּֽעֲתָ֑תְנִי\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb*
\q1 \rb The twilight|נֶ֣שֶׁף\rb* \rb I desired|חִשְׁקִ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb has turned|שָׂ֥ם\rb* \rb to horror.|לַחֲרָדָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb They prepare|עָרֹ֧ךְ\rb* \rb a table,|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֛ן\rb* \rb they lay out|צָפֹ֥ה\rb* \rb a carpet,|הַצָּפִ֖ית\rb*
\q2 \rb they eat,|אָכ֣וֹל\rb* \rb they drink!|שָׁתֹ֑ה\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Rise up,|ק֥וּמוּ\rb* \rb O princes,|הַשָּׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb oil|מִשְׁח֥וּ\rb* \rb the shields!|מָגֵֽן׃פ\rb*
\q2 \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb to me:|אֵלַ֖י\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Go,|לֵ֚ךְ\rb* \rb post|הַעֲמֵ֣ד\rb* \rb a lookout|הַֽמְצַפֶּ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and have him report|יַגִּֽיד׃\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he sees.|יִרְאֶ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb When he sees|וְרָ֣אָה\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֗כֶב\rb* \rb with teams|צֶ֚מֶד\rb* \rb of horsemen,|פָּֽרָשִׁ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb riders|רֶ֥כֶב\rb* \rb on donkeys,|חֲמ֖וֹר\rb* \rb riders|רֶ֣כֶב\rb* \rb on camels,|גָּמָ֑ל\rb*
\q2 \rb he must be alert,|וְהִקְשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |קֶ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb fully|רַב־\rb* \rb alert.”|קָֽשֶׁב׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Then the lookout|אַרְיֵ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 21:8 \ft DSS and Syriac; MT \fqa lion\f* \rb shouted:|וַיִּקְרָ֖א\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Day|תָּמִיד֙\rb* \rb after day,|יוֹמָ֔ם\rb* \rb my lord,|אֲדֹנָ֗י\rb*
\q2 \rb I|אָנֹכִ֞י\rb* \rb stand|עֹמֵ֤ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the watchtower;|מִצְפֶּ֣ה׀\rb*
\q1 \rb night after|כָּל־\rb* \rb night|הַלֵּילֽוֹת׃\rb*
\q2 \rb I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb stay|נִצָּ֖ב\rb* \rb at|וְעַל־\rb* \rb my post.|מִ֨שְׁמַרְתִּ֔י\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb Look,|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb here|זֶ֥ה\rb* \rb come|בָא֙\rb* \rb the riders,|רֶ֣כֶב\rb*\rb |אִ֔ישׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb horsemen|פָּֽרָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb in pairs.”|צֶ֖מֶד\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb And one answered,|וַיַּ֣עַן\rb* \rb saying:|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Fallen,|נָפְלָ֤ה\rb* \rb fallen is|נָֽפְלָה֙\rb* \rb Babylon!|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb*\f + \fr 21:9 \ft See \ref Revelation 14:8|REV 14:8\ref* and Revelation 18:2.\f*
\q2 \rb All|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the images|פְּסִילֵ֥י\rb* \rb of her gods|אֱלֹהֶ֖יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb lie shattered|שִׁבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb on the ground!”|לָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb O my people,|וּבֶן־\rb* \rb crushed|מְדֻשָׁתִ֖י\rb* \rb on the threshing floor,|גָּרְנִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb I tell|הִגַּ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb you|לָכֶֽם׃ס\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have heard|שָׁמַ֗עְתִּי\rb*
\q1 \rb from|מֵאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֧ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֛וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*
\s1 The Burden against Edom
\r \ref Isaiah 34:5–17|ISA 34:5-17\ref*)
\p \v 11 \rb This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb against Dumah:|דּוּמָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 21:11 \fqa Dumah \ft is a wordplay on \fqa Edom\ft , meaning \fqa silence\ft .\f*
\b 
\q1 \rb One calls|קֹרֵ֣א\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb from Seir,|מִשֵּׂעִ֔יר\rb*\f + \fr 21:11 \fqa Seir \ft is another name for Edom.\f*
\q2 \rb “Watchman,|שֹׁמֵר֙\rb* \rb what is left|מַה־\rb* \rb of the night?|מִלַּ֔יְלָה\rb*
\q2 \rb Watchman,|שֹׁמֵ֖ר\rb* \rb what is left|מַה־\rb* \rb of the night?”|מִלֵּֽיל׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb The watchman|שֹׁמֵ֔ר\rb* \rb replies,|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
\q2 \rb “Morning|בֹ֖קֶר\rb* \rb has come,|אָתָ֥ה\rb* \rb but also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb the night.|לָ֑יְלָה\rb*
\q1 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb you would inquire,|תִּבְעָי֥וּן\rb* \rb then inquire.|בְּעָ֖יוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb Come back|אֵתָֽיוּ׃ס\rb* \rb yet again.”|שֻׁ֥בוּ\rb*
\s1 The Burden against Arabia
\p \v 13 \rb This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb against Arabia:|בַּעְרָ֑ב\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb In the thickets|בַּיַּ֤עַר\rb* \rb of Arabia|בַּעְרַב֙\rb* \rb you must lodge,|תָּלִ֔ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb O caravans|אֹֽרְח֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Dedanites.|דְּדָנִֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb |לִקְרַ֥את\rb* \rb Bring|הֵתָ֣יוּ\rb* \rb water|מָ֑יִם\rb* \rb for the thirsty,|צָמֵ֖א\rb*
\q2 \rb O dwellers|יֹשְׁבֵי֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Tema;|תֵּימָ֔א\rb*
\q2 \rb meet|קִדְּמ֥וּ\rb* \rb the refugees|נֹדֵֽד׃\rb* \rb with food.|בְּלַחְמ֖וֹ\rb*
\q1 \v 15 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they flee|נָדָ֑דוּ\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the sword—|חֲרָב֖וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb |מִפְּנֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb that is drawn—|נְטוּשָׁ֗ה\rb*
\q1 \rb from|וּמִפְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the bow|קֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb that is bent,|דְּרוּכָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and from|וּמִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the stress|כֹּ֥בֶד\rb* \rb of battle.|מִלְחָמָֽה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֛ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֖י\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb to me:|אֵלָ֑י\rb*\rb |בְּע֤וֹד\rb* \rb “Within one year,|שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb as a hired worker|שָׂכִ֔יר\rb* \rb would count it,|כִּשְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the glory|כְּב֥וֹד\rb* \rb of Kedar|קֵדָֽר׃\rb* \rb will be gone.|וְכָלָ֖ה\rb* \v 17 \rb The remaining|וּשְׁאָ֧ר\rb*\rb |מִסְפַּר־\rb* \rb archers,|קֶ֛שֶׁת\rb* \rb the warriors|גִּבּוֹרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Kedar,|קֵדָ֖ר\rb* \rb will be few.”|יִמְעָ֑טוּ\rb*
\p \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb has spoken.|דִּבֵּֽר׃ס\rb*
\c 22
\s1 The Valley of Vision
\p \v 1 \rb This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb against the Valley|גֵּ֣יא\rb* \rb of Vision:|חִזָּי֑וֹן\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb ails you now,|אֵפ֔וֹא\rb*
\q2 \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you have all|כֻּלָּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb gone up|עָלִ֥ית\rb* \rb to the rooftops,|לַגַּגּֽוֹת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb O city|עִ֚יר\rb* \rb of commotion,|תְּשֻׁא֣וֹת׀\rb*\rb |מְלֵאָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb O town|קִרְיָ֖ה\rb*\rb |הֽוֹמִיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb of revelry?|עַלִּיזָ֑ה\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Your slain|חֲלָלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb die|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword,|חֶ֔רֶב\rb*
\q2 \rb nor were they|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb killed|מֵתֵ֥י\rb* \rb in battle.|מִלְחָמָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb your rulers|קְצִינַ֥יִךְ\rb* \rb have fled|נָֽדְדוּ־\rb* \rb together,|יַ֖חַד\rb*
\q2 \rb captured|אֻסָּ֑רוּ\rb* \rb without a bow.|מִקֶּ֣שֶׁת\rb*
\q1 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb your fugitives|נִמְצָאַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb were captured|אֻסְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb together,|יַחְדָּ֔ו\rb*
\q2 \rb having fled|בָּרָֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb to a distant place.|מֵרָח֖וֹק\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb I said,|אָמַ֛רְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb “Turn away|שְׁע֥וּ\rb* \rb from me,|מִנִּ֖י\rb* \rb let me weep|בַּבֶּ֑כִי\rb* \rb bitterly!|אֲמָרֵ֣ר\rb*
\q1 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb try|תָּאִ֣יצוּ\rb* \rb to console me|לְנַֽחֲמֵ֔נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the destruction|שֹׁ֖ד\rb* \rb of the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of my people.”|עַמִּֽי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the Lord|לַֽאדֹנָ֧י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֛ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb has set a day|יוֹם֩\rb*
