\s1 A Message for Shebna
\p \v 15 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֖ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֑וֹת\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb “Go,|לֶךְ־\rb* \rb say|בֹּא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shebna,|שֶׁבְנָ֖א\rb* \rb the|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb steward|הַסֹּכֵ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the palace:|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \v 16 \rb What|מַה־\rb* \rb are you|לְּךָ֥\rb* \rb doing here,|פֹה֙\rb* \rb and who|וּמִ֣י\rb* \rb authorized you|פֹ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb to carve out|חָצַ֧בְתָּ\rb* \rb a tomb|קָ֑בֶר\rb* \rb for yourself|לְּךָ֛\rb* \rb here—|פֹּ֖ה\rb*  \rb to chisel|חֹצְבִ֤י\rb* \rb your tomb|קִבְר֔וֹ\rb* \rb in the height|מָרוֹם֙\rb* \rb and cut|חֹקְקִ֥י\rb* \rb your resting place|מִשְׁכָּ֥ן\rb* \rb in the rock?|בַסֶּ֖לַע\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Look,|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb O mighty man!|גָּ֑בֶר\rb* \rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb is about to shake you violently.|מְטַלְטֶלְךָ֔\rb*\rb |טַלְטֵלָ֖ה\rb* \rb He will take hold|וְעֹטְךָ֖\rb* \rb of you,|עָטֹֽה׃\rb* \v 18 \rb roll you|צָנ֤וֹף\rb*\rb |יִצְנָפְךָ֙\rb*\rb |צְנֵפָ֔ה\rb* \rb into a ball,|כַּדּ֕וּר\rb* \rb and sling you into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a wide|רַחֲבַ֣ת\rb*\rb |יָדָ֑יִם\rb* \rb land.|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb There|שָׁ֣מָּה\rb* \rb you will die,|תָמ֗וּת\rb* \rb and there|וְשָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb your glorious|כְּבוֹדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb chariots will remain—|מַרְכְּב֣וֹת\rb* \rb a disgrace|קְל֖וֹן\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of your master.|אֲדֹנֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 19 \rb I will remove you|וַהֲדַפְתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from office,|מִמַּצָּבֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb and you will be ousted|יֶהֶרְסֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb from your position.|וּמִמַּעֲמָֽדְךָ֖\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb |וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb On that|הַה֑וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will summon|וְקָרָ֣אתִי\rb* \rb My servant,|לְעַבְדִּ֔י\rb* \rb Eliakim|לְאֶלְיָקִ֖ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hilkiah.|חִלְקִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 21 \rb I will clothe him|וְהִלְבַּשְׁתִּ֣יו\rb* \rb with your robe|כֻּתָּנְתֶּ֗ךָ\rb* \rb and tie your sash|וְאַבְנֵֽטְךָ֙\rb* \rb around him.|אֲחַזְּקֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb I will put|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb your authority|וּמֶֽמְשֶׁלְתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb in his hand,|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb and he will be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb a father|לְאָ֛ב\rb* \rb to the dwellers|לְיוֹשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb and to the house|וּלְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 22 \rb I will place|וְנָתַתִּ֛י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his shoulder|שִׁכְמ֑וֹ\rb* \rb the key|מַפְתֵּ֥חַ\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of David.|דָּוִ֖ד\rb* \rb What he opens|וּפָתַח֙\rb* \rb no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb one can shut,|סֹגֵ֔ר\rb* \rb and what he shuts|וְסָגַ֖ר\rb* \rb no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one can open.|פֹּתֵֽחַ׃\rb*\f + \fr 22:22 \ft See \ref Revelation 3:7|REV 3:7\ref*.\f* \v 23 \rb I will drive him|וּתְקַעְתִּ֥יו\rb* \rb like a peg|יָתֵ֖ד\rb* \rb into a firm|נֶאֱמָ֑ן\rb* \rb place,|בְּמָק֣וֹם\rb* \rb and he will be|וְהָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb a throne|לְכִסֵּ֥א\rb* \rb of glory|כָב֖וֹד\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of his father.|אָבִֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb So they will hang|וְתָל֨וּ\rb* \rb on him|עָלָ֜יו\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the glory|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb of his father’s|אָבִ֗יו\rb* \rb house:|בֵּית־\rb* \rb the descendants|הַצֶּֽאֱצָאִים֙\rb* \rb and the offshoots—|וְהַצְּפִע֔וֹת\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the lesser|הַקָּטָ֑ן\rb*\rb |מִכְּלֵי֙\rb* \rb vessels,|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb from bowls|הָֽאַגָּנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb to|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb every kind|כָּל־\rb*\rb |כְּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of jar.|הַנְּבָלִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb In that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day,|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb* \rb the peg|הַיָּתֵ֔ד\rb* \rb driven|הַתְּקוּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb into a firm|נֶאֱמָ֑ן\rb* \rb place|בְּמָק֣וֹם\rb* \rb will give way;|תָּמוּשׁ֙\rb* \rb it will be sheared off|וְנִגְדְּעָ֣ה\rb* \rb and fall,|וְנָפְלָ֗ה\rb* \rb and the load|הַמַּשָּׂ֣א\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb upon it|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb will be cut down.”|וְנִכְרַת֙\rb*
\p \rb Indeed,|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has spoken.|דִּבֵּֽר׃ס\rb*
\c 23
\s1 The Burden against Tyre
\r \ref Ezekiel 26:1–21|EZK 26:1-21\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb This is the burden|מַשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb against Tyre:|צֹ֑ר\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb Wail,|הֵילִ֣ילוּ׀\rb* \rb O ships|אֳנִיּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Tarshish,|תַּרְשִׁ֗ישׁ\rb*\f + \fr 23:1 \ft Or \fqa Wail, O fleet of trading ships\ft ; also in verse 14\f*
