\q1 \rb the harvest|קְצִ֥יר\rb* \rb of the Nile|יְא֖וֹר\rb* \rb was the revenue of Tyre;|תְּבֽוּאָתָ֑הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb she was|וַתְּהִ֖י\rb* \rb the merchant|סְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the nations.|גּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Be ashamed,|בּ֣וֹשִׁי\rb* \rb O Sidon,|צִיד֔וֹן\rb* \rb the stronghold|מָע֥וֹז\rb* \rb of the sea,|יָ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb has spoken:|אָמַ֣ר\rb*
\q1 \rb “I have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb been in labor|חַ֣לְתִּי\rb*
\q2 \rb or given birth.|יָלַ֗דְתִּי\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb*
\q1 \rb I have not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb raised|גִדַּ֛לְתִּי\rb* \rb young men|בַּחוּרִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb or brought up|רוֹמַ֥מְתִּי\rb* \rb young women.”|בְתוּלֽוֹת׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb When|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the report reaches|שֵׁ֖מַע\rb* \rb Egypt,|לְמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb they will writhe in agony|יָחִ֖ילוּ\rb* \rb over the news|כְּשֵׁ֥מַע\rb* \rb of Tyre.|צֹֽר׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Cross over|עִבְר֖וּ\rb* \rb to Tarshish;|תַּרְשִׁ֑ישָׁה\rb*
\q2 \rb wail,|הֵילִ֖ילוּ\rb* \rb O inhabitants|יֹ֥שְׁבֵי\rb* \rb of the coastland!|אִֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb Is this|הֲזֹ֥את\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb jubilant city,|עַלִּיזָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb whose origin|קַדְמָתָהּ֙\rb* \rb is from antiquity,|קֶ֤דֶם\rb*\rb |מִֽימֵי־\rb*
\q1 \rb whose feet|רַגְלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb have taken her|יֹבִל֣וּהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb to settle|לָגֽוּר׃\rb* \rb far away?|מֵֽרָח֖וֹק\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb Who|מִ֚י\rb* \rb planned|יָעַ֣ץ\rb* \rb this|זֹ֔את\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Tyre,|צֹ֖ר\rb*
\q2 \rb the bestower of crowns,|הַמַּֽעֲטִירָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb traders|סֹחֲרֶ֙יה֙\rb* \rb are princes,|שָׂרִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb whose merchants|כִּנְעָנֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb are renowned|נִכְבַּדֵּי־\rb* \rb on the earth?|אָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb planned it,|יְעָצָ֑הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb to defile|לְחַלֵּל֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its glorious|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb beauty,|צְבִ֔י\rb*
