\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb In the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבַּע֩\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֨ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֜ה\rb* \rb of Hezekiah’s|חִזְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb reign,|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֤יב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁוּר֙\rb*\rb |עַ֣ל\rb* \rb attacked|עָלָ֞ה\rb* \rb and captured|וַֽיִּתְפְּשֵֽׂם׃\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fortified|הַבְּצֻר֖וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \v 2 \rb And the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֣וּר׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabshakeh,|שָׁקֵ֨ה\rb*\f + \fr 36:2 \ft Hebrew \fqa Rabshakeh \ft is the title of a high-ranking Assyrian military officer; here and throughout chapters 36 and 37, as well as 2 Kings 18 and 19\f* \rb with a great|כָּבֵ֑ד\rb* \rb army,|בְּחֵ֣יל\rb* \rb from Lachish|מִלָּכִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb at Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלְַ֛מָה\rb* \rb And he stopped|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֗ד\rb* \rb by the aqueduct|בִּתְעָלַת֙\rb* \rb of the upper|הָעֶלְיוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb pool,|הַבְּרֵכָ֣ה\rb* \rb on the road|בִּמְסִלַּ֖ת\rb* \rb to the Launderer’s|כוֹבֵֽס׃\rb* \rb Field.|שְׂדֵ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then Eliakim|אֶלְיָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the palace|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb administrator,|עַל־\rb* \rb Shebna|וְשֶׁבְנָא֙\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb and Joah|וְיוֹאָ֥ח\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Asaph|אָסָ֖ף\rb* \rb the recorder,|הַמַּזְכִּֽיר׃\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to him.|אֵלָ֛יו\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb |רַב־\rb* \rb The Rabshakeh|שָׁקֵ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb “Tell|אִמְרוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb king,|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria,|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb What|מָ֧ה\rb* \rb is the basis|בָּטָֽחְתָּ׃\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb confidence|הַבִּטָּח֛וֹן\rb* \rb of yours?|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \v 5 \rb You claim to have|אָמַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb*\f + \fr 36:5 \ft Literally \fqa You speak\ft ; see DSS and \ref 2 Kings 18:20|2KI 18:20\ref*; MT \fqa I speak\ft .\f* \rb a strategy|עֵצָ֥ה\rb* \rb and strength|וּגְבוּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb for war,|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb but|אַךְ־\rb* \rb these are empty|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb words.|שְׂפָתַ֔יִם\rb* \rb In|עַל־\rb* \rb whom|מִ֣י\rb* \rb are you now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb trusting,|בָטַ֔חְתָּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have rebelled|מָרַ֖דְתָּ\rb* \rb against me?|בִּֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Look now,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb you are trusting|בָטַ֡חְתָּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb that|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb splintered|הָרָצ֤וּץ\rb* \rb reed|הַקָּנֶ֨ה\rb* \rb of a staff|מִשְׁעֶנֶת֩\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |וּבָ֥א\rb* \rb will pierce|וּנְקָבָ֑הּ\rb* \rb the hand|בְכַפּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of anyone|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb who leans|יִסָּמֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb on it.|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb Such is|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to all|לְכָֽל־\rb* \rb who trust|הַבֹּטְחִ֖ים\rb* \rb in him.|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 7 \rb But if|וְכִי־\rb* \rb you say|תֹאמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb ‘We trust|בָּטָ֑חְנוּ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God,’|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb is He|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb not|הֲלוֹא־\rb* \rb the One|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb whose high places|בָּמֹתָ֣יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and altars|מִזְבְּחֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has removed,|הֵסִ֤יר\rb* \rb saying|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Judah|לִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem,|וְלִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb ‘You must worship|תִּֽשְׁתַּחֲוֽוּ׃\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֛י\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb altar’?|הַמִּזְבֵּ֥חַ\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Now, therefore,|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb make a bargain|הִתְעָ֣רֶב\rb*\rb |נָ֔א\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb my master,|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria.|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb I will give|וְאֶתְּנָ֤ה\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb two thousand|אַלְפַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb horses—|סוּסִ֔ים\rb*  \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you can|תּוּכַ֕ל\rb* \rb put|לָ֥תֶת\rb* \rb riders|רֹכְבִ֥ים\rb* \rb on them!|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb For how|וְאֵ֣יךְ\rb* \rb can you repel|תָּשִׁ֗יב\rb*\rb |אֵ֠ת\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb a single|אַחַ֛ד\rb* \rb officer|פַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb among the least|הַקְטַנִּ֑ים\rb* \rb of my master’s|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb when you depend|וַתִּבְטַ֤ח\rb*\rb |לְךָ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb for chariots|לְרֶ֖כֶב\rb* \rb and horsemen?|וּלְפָרָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \v 10 \rb So now,|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb was it apart from|הֲמִבַּלְעֲדֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that I have come up|עָלִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb to destroy it?|לְהַשְׁחִיתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb The LORD Himself|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb ‘Go up|עֲלֵ֛ה\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb and destroy it.’”|וְהַשְׁחִיתָֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Then Eliakim,|אֶלְיָקִים֩\rb* \rb Shebna,|וְשֶׁבְנָ֨א\rb* \rb and Joah|וְיוֹאָ֜ח\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabshakeh,|שָׁקֵ֗ה\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֤א\rb* \rb speak|דַּבֶּר־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb in Aramaic,|אֲרָמִ֔ית\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we|אֲנָ֑חְנוּ\rb* \rb understand it.|שֹׁמְעִ֖ים\rb* \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb speak|תְּדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to us|אֵלֵ֙ינוּ֙\rb* \rb in Hebrew|יְהוּדִ֔ית\rb*\f + \fr 36:11 \ft Or \fqa in the dialect of Judah\ft ; also in verse 13\f* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wall.”|הַחוֹמָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb |רַב־\rb* \rb But the Rabshakeh|שָׁקֵ֗ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Has my master|אֲדֹנֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb sent me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb only to|הַאֶ֨ל\rb* \rb you and|וְאֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb your master,|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb and not|הֲלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb sitting|הַיֹּֽשְׁבִים֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wall,|הַ֣חוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb who are destined with you|עִמָּכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their own dung|חַרְאֵיהֶם\rb* \rb and drink|וְלִשְׁתּ֛וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their own urine?”|שֵׁינֵיהֶם\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb |רַב־\rb* \rb Then the Rabshakeh|שָׁקֵ֔ה\rb* \rb stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb and called out|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb loudly|בְקוֹל־\rb*\rb |גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb in Hebrew:|יְהוּדִ֑ית\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Hear|שִׁמְע֗וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֛י\rb* \rb of the great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb king,|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria!|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb* \v 14 \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb deceive|יַשִּׁ֥א\rb* \rb you,|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he cannot|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb deliver|לְהַצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb you.|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb let Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb persuade you to trust|יַבְטַ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb in the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb when he says,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘The LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb will surely deliver us;|הַצֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |יַצִּילֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be given|תִנָּתֵן֙\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria.’|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb listen|תִּשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּס\rb* \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֨ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֗וּר\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֜ר\rb* \rb Make|עֲשֽׂוּ־\rb* \rb peace|בְרָכָה֙\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֤י\rb*\f + \fr 36:16 \ft Or \fqa Make a blessing with me\f* \rb and come out|וּצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb to me.|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb Then every one of you|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb will eat|וְאִכְל֤וּ\rb* \rb from his own vine|גַּפְנוֹ֙\rb* \rb and|וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb his own fig tree,|תְּאֵנָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and drink|וּשְׁת֖וּ\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb water|מֵי־\rb* \rb from his own cistern,|בוֹרֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 17 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb I come|בֹּאִ֕י\rb* \rb and take you away|וְלָקַחְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb like your own—|כְּאַרְצְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of grain|דָּגָן֙\rb* \rb and new wine,|וְתִיר֔וֹשׁ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb and vineyards.|וּכְרָמִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Do not let|פֶּן־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb mislead|יַסִּ֨ית\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb you when he says,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will deliver us.’|יַצִּילֵ֑נוּ\rb* \rb Has the god|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of any|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb nation|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb ever delivered|הַהִצִּ֜ילוּ\rb* \rb his land|אַרְצ֔וֹ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria?|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb* \v 19 \rb Where|אַיֵּ֞ה\rb* \rb are the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Hamath|חֲמָת֙\rb* \rb and Arpad?|וְאַרְפָּ֔ד\rb* \rb Where|אַיֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb are the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Sepharvaim?|סְפַרְוָ֑יִם\rb*\rb |וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb Have they delivered|הִצִּ֥ילוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Samaria|שֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb from my hand?|מִיָּדִֽי׃\rb* \v 20 \rb Who|מִ֗י\rb* \rb among all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb lands|הָֽאֲרָצוֹת֙\rb* \rb has delivered|הִצִּ֥ילוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his land|אַרְצָ֖ם\rb* \rb from my hand?|מִיָּדִ֑י\rb* \rb How then|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb can the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb deliver|יַצִּ֧יל\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb from my hand?”|מִיָּדִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb But the people remained silent|וַֽיַּחֲרִ֔ישׁוּ\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb answer a word,|עָנ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הִ֛יא\rb* \rb had commanded,|מִצְוַ֨ת\rb* \rb “Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb answer him.”|תַעֲנֻֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Then Hilkiah’s|חִלְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Eliakim|אֶלְיָקִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the palace|הַ֠בַּיִת\rb* \rb administrator,|עַל־\rb* \rb Shebna|וְשֶׁבְנָ֨א\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסּוֹפֵ֜ר\rb* \rb and Asaph’s|אָסָ֧ף\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Joah|וְיוֹאָ֨ח\rb* \rb the recorder|הַמַּזְכִּ֛יר\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with their clothes|בְגָדִ֑ים\rb* \rb torn,|קְרוּעֵ֣י\rb* \rb and they relayed|וַיַּגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb of the Rabshakeh.|שָׁקֵֽה׃ס\rb*
\c 37
\s1 Isaiah’s Message of Deliverance
\r \ref 2 Kings 19:1–7|2KI 19:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb On|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb hearing this report,|כִּשְׁמֹ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb tore|וַיִּקְרַ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothes,|בְּגָדָ֑יו\rb* \rb put on|וַיִּתְכַּ֣ס\rb* \rb sackcloth,|בַּשָּׂ֔ק\rb* \rb and entered|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And he sent|וַ֠יִּשְׁלַח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eliakim|אֶלְיָקִ֨ים\rb* \rb the palace|הַבַּ֜יִת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb administrator,|עַל־\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb Shebna|שֶׁבְנָ֣א\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסּוֹפֵ֗ר\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and the leading|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb all wearing|מִתְכַּסִּ֖ים\rb* \rb sackcloth,|בַּשַּׂקִּ֑ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִֽיא׃\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amoz|אָמ֖וֹץ\rb* \v 3 \rb to tell|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb him,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Today|יוֹם־\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb is a day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb of distress,|צָרָ֧ה\rb* \rb rebuke,|וְתוֹכֵחָ֛ה\rb* \rb and disgrace;|וּנְאָצָ֖ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb children|בָנִים֙\rb* \rb have come|בָ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to the point of|עַד־\rb* \rb birth,|מַשְׁבֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb but there is no|אַ֖יִן\rb* \rb strength|וְכֹ֥חַ\rb* \rb to deliver them.|לְלֵדָֽה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֡י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמַע֩\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb of the Rabshakeh,|שָׁקֵ֗ה\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָיו֙\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֤וּר׀\rb* \rb has sent|שְׁלָח֨וֹ\rb* \rb to defy|לְחָרֵף֙\rb* \rb the living|חַ֔י\rb* \rb God,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb and He will rebuke him|וְהוֹכִ֙יחַ֙\rb* \rb for the words|בַּדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb has heard.|שָׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb Therefore lift up|וְנָשָׂ֣אתָ\rb* \rb a prayer|תְפִלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb for|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb the remnant|הַשְּׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb that still survives.”|הַנִּמְצָאָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So the servants|עַבְדֵ֛י\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Isaiah,|יְשַׁעְיָֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb who|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “Tell|תֹאמְר֖וּן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your master|אֲדֹנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָא֙\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִים֙\rb* \rb you have heard,|שָׁמַ֔עְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the servants|נַעֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֖וּר\rb*\rb |אוֹתִֽי׃\rb* \rb have blasphemed Me.|גִּדְּפ֛וּ\rb* \v 7 \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I will put|נוֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb a spirit|ר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb in him|בּוֹ֙\rb* \rb so that he will hear|וְשָׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb a rumor|שְׁמוּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and return|וְשָׁ֣ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his own land,|אַרְצ֑וֹ\rb* \rb where|בְּאַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb I will cause him to fall|וְהִפַּלְתִּ֥יו\rb* \rb by the sword.’”|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb*
\s1 Sennacherib’s Blasphemous Letter
\r \ref 2 Kings 19:8–13|2KI 19:8-13\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb When|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabshakeh|שָׁקֵ֔ה\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the king of Assyria had left|נָסַ֖ע\rb* \rb Lachish,|מִלָּכִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb he withdrew|וַיָּ֙שָׁב֙\rb* \rb and found|וַיִּמְצָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb fighting|נִלְחָ֖ם\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Libnah.|לִבְנָ֑ה\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Now Sennacherib had been warned|וַיִּשְׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb about|עַל־\rb* \rb Tirhakah|תִּרְהָ֤קָה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Cush:|כּוּשׁ֙\rb*\f + \fr 37:9 \ft That is, the upper Nile region\f* \rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*\rb “He has set out|יָצָ֖א\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb against you.”|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\p \rb On hearing this,|וַיִּשְׁמַע֙\rb* \rb Sennacherib sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 10 \rb “Give this message|תֹאמְר֗וּן\rb*\rb |כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah:|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*
\pmo \rb ‘Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb in whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb trust,|בּוֹטֵ֥חַ\rb* \rb deceive you|יַשִּֽׁאֲךָ֣\rb* \rb by saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb that Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be delivered|תִנָּתֵן֙\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria.|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb* \v 11 \rb Surely|הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb have heard|שָׁמַ֗עְתָּ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֛וּר\rb* \rb have done|עָשׂ֜וּ\rb* \rb to all the other|לְכָל־\rb* \rb countries,|הָאֲרָצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb devoting them to destruction.|לְהַחֲרִימָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 37:11 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb Will you then|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb be spared?|תִּנָּצֵֽל׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Did the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb destroyed|הִשְׁחִ֣יתוּ\rb* \rb by my fathers|אֲבוֹתַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb rescue those nations—|הַהִצִּ֨ילוּ\rb* \rb the gods of|אוֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb Gozan,|גּוֹזָ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Haran,|חָרָ֑ן\rb* \rb and Rezeph,|וְרֶ֥צֶף\rb* \rb and of the people|וּבְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֶ֖דֶן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Telassar?|בִּתְלַשָּֽׂר׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Where|אַיֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb are the kings|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Hamath,|חֲמָת֙\rb*\rb |וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Arpad,|אַרְפָּ֔ד\rb*\rb |וּמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb Sepharvaim,|סְפַרְוָ֑יִם\rb* \rb Hena,|הֵנַ֖ע\rb* \rb and Ivvah?’”|וְעִוָּֽה׃\rb*
\s1 Hezekiah’s Prayer
\r \ref 2 Kings 19:14–19|2KI 19:14-19\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb So Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֧הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb received|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the letter|הַסְּפָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb the messengers,|הַמַּלְאָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb read it,|וַיִּקְרָאֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and went up|וַיַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and spread it out|וַיִּפְרְשֵׂ֥הוּ\rb*\rb |חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 15 \rb And Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּל֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD:|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*
\pmo \v 16 \rb “O LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb of Hosts,|צְבָא֜וֹת\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb enthroned|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb above the cherubim,|הַכְּרֻבִ֔ים\rb* \rb You|אַתָּה־\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדְּךָ֔\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb* \rb are God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb over all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb made|עָשִׂ֔יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 17 \rb Incline|הַטֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb Your ear,|אָזְנְךָ֙\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb and hear;|וּֽשְׁמָ֔ע\rb* \rb open|פְּקַ֧ח\rb* \rb Your eyes,|עֵינֶ֖ךָ\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb and see.|וּרְאֵ֑ה\rb* \rb Listen to|וּשְׁמַ֗ע\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֔יב\rb* \rb has sent|שָׁלַ֔ח\rb* \rb to defy|לְחָרֵ֖ף\rb* \rb the living|חָֽי׃\rb* \rb God.|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*
\b 
\pmo \v 18 \rb Truly,|אָמְנָ֖ם\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֛וּר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have laid waste|הֶחֱרִ֜יבוּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these countries|הָאֲרָצ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and their lands.|אַרְצָֽם׃\rb* \v 19 \rb They have cast|וְנָתֹ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their gods|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into the fire|בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb and destroyed them,|וַֽיְאַבְּדֽוּם׃\rb* \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb they|הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb were not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb but only|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb wood|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb and stone—|וָאֶ֖בֶן\rb*  \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֧ה\rb* \rb of human|אָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb hands.|יְדֵֽי־\rb*
\b 
