\s1 Hezekiah’s Illness and Recovery
\r \ref 2 Kings 20:1–11|2KI 20:1-11\ref*; \ref 2 Chronicles 32:24–31|2CH 32:24-31\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb became mortally|לָמ֑וּת\rb* \rb ill.|חָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb The prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amoz|אָמ֜וֹץ\rb* \rb came|וַיָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb to him|אֵ֠לָיו\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘Put your house|לְבֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb in order,|צַ֣ו\rb* \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are about to die;|מֵ֥ת\rb* \rb you will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb recover.’”|תִֽחְיֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Then Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb turned|וַיַּסֵּ֧ב\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wall|הַקִּ֑יר\rb* \rb and prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb saying,|וַיֹּאמַ֗ר\rb* \rb “Please,|אָנָּ֤ה\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb remember|זְכָר־\rb*\rb |נָ֞א\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I have walked|הִתְהַלַּ֣כְתִּי\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb faithfully|בֶּֽאֱמֶת֙\rb* \rb and with wholehearted|וּבְלֵ֣ב\rb* \rb devotion;|שָׁלֵ֔ם\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֑יתִי\rb* \rb what is good|וְהַטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb in Your sight.”|בְּעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb And Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |בְּכִ֥י\rb* \rb wept|וַיֵּ֥בְךְּ\rb* \rb bitterly.|גָדֽוֹל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Isaiah,|יְשַׁעְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 5 \rb “Go|הָל֞וֹךְ\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb David,|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘I have heard|שָׁמַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your prayer;|תְּפִלָּתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb I have seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your tears.|דִּמְעָתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb Behold,|הִנְנִי֙\rb* \rb I will add|יוֹסִ֣ף\rb* \rb fifteen|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb your life.|יָמֶ֔יךָ\rb* \v 6 \rb And I will deliver you|אַצִּ֣ילְךָ֔\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb from the hand|וּמִכַּ֤ף\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria.|אַשּׁוּר֙\rb* \rb I will defend|וְגַנּוֹתִ֖י\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb city.|הָעִ֥יר\rb*\f + \fr 38:6 \ft MT and LXX; DSS includes \fqa for My sake and for the sake of My servant David\ft ; see \ref 2 Kings 20:6|2KI 20:6\ref*.\f* \v 7 \rb This|וְזֶה־\rb* \rb will be a sign|הָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb to you|לְּךָ֥\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb what|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb He has promised:|דִּבֵּֽר׃\rb* \v 8 \rb |הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb I will make|מֵשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb the sun’s|בַּשֶּׁ֛מֶשׁ\rb* \rb shadow|צֵ֣ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb falls|יָרְדָה֩\rb* \rb on the stairway|הַֽמַּעֲל֡וֹת\rb* \rb of Ahaz|אָחָ֥ז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb go back|אֲחֹרַנִּ֖ית\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb steps.’”|מַעֲל֑וֹת\rb*
\p \rb So the sunlight|הַשֶּׁ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb went back|וַתָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb the ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb*\rb |מַעֲל֔וֹת\rb* \rb steps|בַּֽמַּעֲל֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb it had descended.|יָרָֽדָה׃ס\rb*
\s1 Hezekiah’s Song of Thanksgiving
\p \v 9 \rb This is a writing|מִכְתָּ֖ב\rb* \rb by Hezekiah|לְחִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb after his illness|בַּחֲלֹת֕וֹ\rb* \rb and recovery:|וַיְחִ֖י\rb*\rb |מֵחָלְיֽוֹ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb said,|אָמַ֗רְתִּי\rb* \rb “In the prime|בִּדְמִ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 38:10 \ft Or \fqa In the quiet \ft or \fqa In the middle\f* \rb of my life|יָמַ֛י\rb*
\q2 \rb I must go|אֵלֵ֖כָה\rb* \rb through the gates|בְּשַׁעֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Sheol|שְׁא֑וֹל\rb*
\q2 \rb and be deprived|פֻּקַּ֖דְתִּי\rb* \rb of the remainder|יֶ֥תֶר\rb* \rb of my years.”|שְׁנוֹתָֽי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb I said,|אָמַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb* \rb “I will never again|לֹא־\rb* \rb see|אֶרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the LORD,|יָ֔הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb even the LORD,|יָ֖הּ\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the living;|הַחַיִּ֑ים\rb*
\q1 \rb I will no|לֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb look on|אַבִּ֥יט\rb* \rb mankind|אָדָ֛ם\rb*
\q2 \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb those who dwell|י֥וֹשְׁבֵי\rb* \rb in this world.|חָֽדֶל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 12 \rb My dwelling|דּוֹרִ֗י\rb* \rb has been picked up|נִסַּ֧ע\rb* \rb and removed|וְנִגְלָ֛ה\rb* \rb from me|מִנִּ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb like a shepherd’s|רֹעִ֑י\rb* \rb tent.|כְּאֹ֣הֶל\rb*
\q1 \rb I have rolled up|קִפַּ֨דְתִּי\rb* \rb my life|חַיַּי֙\rb* \rb like a weaver;|כָאֹרֵ֤ג\rb*
\q2 \rb He cuts me off|יְבַצְּעֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb from the loom;|מִדַּלָּ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb from day|מִיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb night|לַ֖יְלָה\rb* \rb You make an end of me.|תַּשְׁלִימֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb I composed myself|שִׁוִּ֤יתִי\rb*\f + \fr 38:13 \ft Or \fqa I cried out\ft ; see Targum Yonaton.\f* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the morning.|בֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb Like a lion|כָּֽאֲרִ֔י\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb He breaks|יְשַׁבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my bones;|עַצְמוֹתָ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb from day|מִיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb night|לַ֖יְלָה\rb* \rb You make an end of me.|תַּשְׁלִימֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb I chirp|אֲצַפְצֵ֔ף\rb* \rb like a swallow|כְּס֤וּס\rb* \rb or crane;|עָגוּר֙\rb*\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb*
\q2 \rb I moan|אֶהְגֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb like a dove.|כַּיּוֹנָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb My eyes|עֵינַי֙\rb* \rb grow weak|דַּלּ֤וּ\rb* \rb as I look upward.|לַמָּר֔וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb O Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֖י\rb* \rb I am oppressed;|עָֽשְׁקָה־\rb* \rb be my security.”|עָרְבֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb What|מָֽה־\rb* \rb can I say?|אֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb*
\q2 \rb He has spoken|וְאָֽמַר־\rb* \rb to me,|לִ֖י\rb* \rb and He Himself|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb has done this.|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb I will walk slowly|אֶדַּדֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb my years|שְׁנוֹתַ֖י\rb*
\q2 \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb the anguish|מַ֥ר\rb* \rb of my soul.|נַפְשִֽׁי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb O Lord,|אֲדֹנָ֖י\rb* \rb by such things|עֲלֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb men live,|יִֽחְי֑וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and in all|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb of them|בָּהֶן֙\rb* \rb my spirit|רוּחִ֔י\rb* \rb finds life.|חַיֵּ֣י\rb*
\q1 \rb You have restored me to health|וְתַחֲלִימֵ֖נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb and have let me live.|וְהַחֲיֵֽנִי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb Surely|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb for my own welfare|לְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb*
\q2 \rb I had such great|מַר־\rb* \rb anguish;|מָ֑ר\rb*
\q1 \rb but Your|וְאַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb love|חָשַׁ֤קְתָּ\rb* \rb has delivered me|נַפְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb from the pit|מִשַּׁ֣חַת\rb* \rb of oblivion,|בְּלִ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb You have cast|הִשְׁלַ֛כְתָּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb my sins|חֲטָאָֽי׃\rb* \rb behind|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb Your back.|גֵוְךָ֖\rb*
\q1 \v 18 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb Sheol|שְׁא֛וֹל\rb* \rb cannot|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb thank You;|תּוֹדֶ֖ךָּ\rb*
\q2 \rb Death|מָ֣וֶת\rb* \rb cannot praise You.|יְהַלְלֶ֑ךָּ\rb*
\q1 \rb Those who descend|יֽוֹרְדֵי־\rb* \rb to the Pit|ב֖וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb hope|יְשַׂבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your faithfulness.|אֲמִתֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 19 \rb The living,|חַ֥י\rb* \rb only the living,|חַ֛י\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb can thank You,|יוֹדֶ֖ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb as I do today;|כָּמ֣וֹנִי\rb*\rb |הַיּ֑וֹם\rb*
\q1 \rb fathers|אָ֣ב\rb* \rb will tell|יוֹדִ֖יעַ\rb* \rb their children|לְבָנִ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb Your faithfulness.|אֲמִתֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 20 \rb The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will save me;|לְהוֹשִׁיעֵ֑נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb we will play songs|נְנַגֵּ֛ן\rb* \rb on stringed instruments|וּנְגִנוֹתַ֧י\rb*
\q1 \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of our lives|חַיֵּ֖ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Now Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb had said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Prepare|יִשְׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb a lump|דְּבֶ֣לֶת\rb* \rb of pressed figs|תְּאֵנִ֑ים\rb* \rb and apply|וְיִמְרְח֥וּ\rb* \rb it to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the boil,|הַשְּׁחִ֖ין\rb* \rb and he will recover.”|וְיֶֽחִי׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb And Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb had asked,|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb “What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb will be the sign|א֑וֹת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I will go up|אֶעֱלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD?”|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\c 39
\s1 Hezekiah Shows His Treasures
\r \ref 2 Kings 20:12–19|2KI 20:12-19\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb At that|הַהִ֡וא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Merodach-baladan|בַּ֠לְאֲדָן\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Baladan|בַּלְאֲדָ֧ן\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֡ח\rb* \rb letters|סְפָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and a gift|וּמִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb for he had heard|וַיִּשְׁמַ֕ע\rb* \rb about|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Hezekiah’s illness|חָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb and recovery.|וַֽיֶּחֱזָֽק׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּהוּ֒\rb* \rb welcomed|וַיִּשְׂמַ֣ח\rb* \rb the envoys gladly|עֲלֵיהֶם֮\rb* \rb and showed them|וַיַּרְאֵ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb what was in his treasure|נְכֹתָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb house—|בֵּ֣ית\rb*  \rb the silver,|הַכֶּסֶף֩\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the gold,|הַזָּהָ֨ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the spices,|הַבְּשָׂמִ֜ים\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb and the precious|הַטּ֗וֹב\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb oil,|הַשֶּׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb as well as his entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb armory—|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |כֵּלָ֔יו\rb* \rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb was found|נִמְצָ֖א\rb* \rb in his storehouses.|בְּאֹֽצְרֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb There was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb nothing|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |דָבָ֗ר\rb* \rb in his palace|בְּבֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb or in all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his dominion|מֶמְשַׁלְתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb that|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb show them.|הֶרְאָ֧ם\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and asked,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb “Where|וּמֵאַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb did those men|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb come from,|יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb and what|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb did they say|אָמְר֣וּ׀\rb*\rb |הָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb to you?”|אֵלָ֜יו\rb*
\p \rb “They came|בָּ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb from|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb a distant|רְחוֹקָ֛ה\rb* \rb land,”|מֵאֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “from Babylon.”|מִבָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb “What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb have they seen|רָא֖וּ\rb* \rb in your palace?”|בְּבֵיתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb Isaiah asked.|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb “They have seen|רָא֔וּ\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb in my palace,”|בְּבֵיתִי֙\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Hezekiah.|חִזְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb “There is nothing|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |הָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |דָבָ֛ר\rb* \rb among my treasures|בְּאוֹצְרֹתָֽי׃\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb show them.”|הִרְאִיתִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb “Hear|שְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts:|צְבָאֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 6 \rb The time|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb will surely|הִנֵּה֮\rb* \rb come|בָּאִים֒\rb* \rb when everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb in your palace|בְּבֵיתֶ֗ךָ\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb and all that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb have stored up|אָצְר֧וּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb will be carried off|וְנִשָּׂ֣א׀\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb Nothing|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb will be left,|יִוָּתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 7 \rb And some of your descendants,|וּמִבָּנֶ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb*\rb |יֵצְא֧וּ\rb* \rb your|מִמְּךָ֛\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb own flesh and blood,|תּוֹלִ֖יד\rb* \rb will be taken away|יִקָּ֑חוּ\rb* \rb to be|וְהָיוּ֙\rb* \rb eunuchs|סָרִיסִ֔ים\rb* \rb in the palace|בְּהֵיכַ֖ל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon.”|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb But Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Isaiah,|יְשַׁעְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb “The word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have spoken|דִּבַּ֑רְתָּ\rb* \rb is good.”|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb For he thought,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “At least|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb there will be|יִהְיֶ֛ה\rb* \rb peace|שָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb and security|וֶאֱמֶ֖ת\rb* \rb in my lifetime.”|בְּיָמָֽי׃פ\rb*
\c 40
\s1 Prepare the Way for the LORD
\r \ref Matthew 3:1–12|MAT 3:1-12\ref*; \ref Mark 1:1–8|MRK 1:1-8\ref*; \ref Luke 3:1–20|LUK 3:1-20\ref*; \ref John 1:19–28|JHN 1:19-28\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb “Comfort,|נַחֲמ֥וּ\rb* \rb comfort|נַחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb My people,”|עַמִּ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb says|יֹאמַ֖ר\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb “Speak|דַּבְּר֞וּ\rb* \rb tenderly to|עַל־\rb*\rb |לֵ֤ב\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְרֽוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and proclaim|וְקִרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb to her|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb*
\q1 \rb that|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb her forced labor|צְבָאָ֔הּ\rb* \rb has been completed;|מָֽלְאָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb her iniquity|עֲוֺנָ֑הּ\rb*\rb |כִּ֤י\rb* \rb has been pardoned.|נִרְצָ֖ה\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she has received|לָקְחָה֙\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb double|כִּפְלַ֖יִם\rb* \rb for all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb her sins.”|חַטֹּאתֶֽיהָ׃ס\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb A voice|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of one calling:|קוֹרֵ֔א\rb*
\b 
\q1 \rb “Prepare|פַּנּ֖וּ\rb* \rb the way|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb for the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb in the wilderness;|בַּמִּדְבָּ֕ר\rb*\f + \fr 40:3 \ft Or \fqa A voice of one calling in the wilderness: “Prepare the way for the LORD\f*
