\q1 \v 4 \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb valley|גֶּיא֙\rb* \rb shall be lifted up,|יִנָּשֵׂ֔א\rb*
\q2 \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb mountain|הַ֥ר\rb* \rb and hill|וְגִבְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb made low;|יִשְׁפָּ֑לוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb the uneven ground|הֶֽעָקֹב֙\rb* \rb will become|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb smooth,|לְמִישׁ֔וֹר\rb*
\q2 \rb and the rugged land|וְהָרְכָסִ֖ים\rb* \rb a plain.|לְבִקְעָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 40:4 \ft LXX \fqa Every valley shall be filled in, and every mountain and hill shall be brought low. All the crooked ways shall become straight, and the rough places plains.\ft Cited in \ref Luke 3:5|LUK 3:5\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 5 \rb And the glory|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb will be revealed,|וְנִגְלָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|כָל־\rb* \rb humanity|בָּשָׂר֙\rb* \rb together|יַחְדָּ֔ו\rb* \rb will see it.”|וְרָא֤וּ\rb*\f + \fr 40:5 \ft Literally \fqa and all flesh together will see it.\ft Cited in \ref Luke 3:6|LUK 3:6\ref*\f*
\qr \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has spoken.|דִּבֵּֽר׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Enduring Word
\r \ref 1 Peter 1:22–25|1PE 1:22-25\ref*)
\q1 \v 6 \rb A voice|ק֚וֹל\rb* \rb says,|אֹמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb “Cry out!”|קְרָ֔א\rb*
\q2 \rb And I asked,|וְאָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb “What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb should I cry out?”|אֶקְרָ֑א\rb*
\q1 \rb “All|כָּל־\rb* \rb flesh|הַבָּשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb is like grass,|חָצִ֔יר\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb its glory|חַסְדּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb like the flowers|כְּצִ֥יץ\rb* \rb of the field.|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb The grass|חָצִיר֙\rb* \rb withers|יָבֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb and the flowers|צִ֔יץ\rb* \rb fall|נָ֣בֵֽל\rb*
\q2 \rb when|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the breath|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb blows|נָ֣שְׁבָה\rb* \rb on them;|בּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb indeed,|אָכֵ֥ן\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \rb are grass.|חָצִ֖יר\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb The grass|חָצִ֖יר\rb* \rb withers|יָבֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and the flowers|צִ֑יץ\rb* \rb fall,|נָ֣בֵֽל\rb*
\q2 \rb but the word|וּדְבַר־\rb* \rb of our God|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb stands|יָק֥וּם\rb* \rb forever.”|לְעוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 40:8 \ft Cited in \ref 1 Peter 1:24–25|1PE 1:24-25\ref*\f*
\s1 Here Is Your God!
\r \ref Romans 11:33–36|ROM 11:33-36\ref*)
\q1 \v 9 \rb Go up|עֲלִי־\rb* \rb on|עַ֣ל\rb* \rb a high|גָּבֹ֤הַ\rb* \rb mountain,|הַר־\rb*
\q2 \rb O Zion,|צִיּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb herald of good news.|מְבַשֶּׂ֣רֶת\rb*
\q1 \rb Raise|הָרִ֤ימִי\rb* \rb your voice loudly,|קוֹלֵ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |בַכֹּ֙חַ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb O Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb herald of good news.|מְבַשֶּׂ֖רֶת\rb*
\q1 \rb Lift it up,|הָרִ֙ימִי֙\rb*\f + \fr 40:9 \ft Or \fqa O herald of good news to Zion, go up on a high mountain. O herald of good news to Jerusalem, lift it up,\f*
\q2 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid!|תִּירָ֔אִי\rb*
\q1 \rb Say|אִמְרִי֙\rb* \rb to the cities|לְעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb “Here|הִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb is your God!”|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
