\q2 \rb they are considered|נֶחְשָׁ֑בוּ\rb*\rb |הֵ֥ן\rb* \rb a speck of dust|וּכְשַׁ֥חַק\rb* \rb on the scales;|מֹאזְנַ֖יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb He lifts up|יִטּֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb the islands|אִיִּ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 40:15 \ft Or \fqa coastlands\f* \rb like fine dust.|כַּדַּ֥ק\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb Lebanon|וּלְבָנ֕וֹן\rb* \rb is not|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb sufficient|דֵּ֖י\rb* \rb for fuel,|בָּעֵ֑ר\rb*
\q2 \rb nor its animals|וְחַיָּת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb enough|דֵּ֖י\rb* \rb for a burnt offering.|עוֹלָֽה׃ס\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb are as nothing|כְּאַ֣יִן\rb* \rb before Him;|נֶגְדּ֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb He regards them|נֶחְשְׁבוּ־\rb* \rb as nothingness|מֵאֶ֥פֶס\rb* \rb and emptiness.|וָתֹ֖הוּ\rb*
\b 
