\q2 \rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb who bears no children;|יָלָ֑דָה\rb*
\q1 \rb break forth|פִּצְחִ֨י\rb* \rb in song|רִנָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and cry aloud,|וְצַהֲלִי֙\rb*
\q2 \rb you who have never|לֹא־\rb* \rb travailed;|חָ֔לָה\rb*
\q1 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb more|רַבִּ֧ים\rb* \rb are the children|בְּֽנֵי־\rb* \rb of the desolate woman|שׁוֹמֵמָ֛ה\rb*
\q2 \rb than|מִבְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of her who has a husband,”|בְעוּלָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 54:1 \ft Cited in \ref Galatians 4:27|GAL 4:27\ref*\f*
\qr \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
