\q2 \rb stretch out|יַטּ֖וּ\rb* \rb the curtains|וִירִיע֧וֹת\rb* \rb of your dwellings,|מִשְׁכְּנוֹתַ֛יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb hold back.|תַּחְשֹׂ֑כִי\rb*
\q1 \rb Lengthen|הַאֲרִ֙יכִי֙\rb* \rb your ropes|מֵֽיתָרַ֔יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and drive your stakes in deep.|וִיתֵדֹתַ֖יִךְ\rb*\f + \fr 54:2 \ft Or \fqa and strengthen your stakes\f*\rb |חַזֵּֽקִי׃\rb*
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb you will spread out|תִּפְרֹ֑צִי\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֥ין\rb* \rb and left;|וּשְׂמֹ֖אול\rb*
\q2 \rb your descendants|וְזַרְעֵךְ֙\rb* \rb will dispossess|יִירָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיִ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb and inhabit|יוֹשִֽׁיבוּ׃\rb* \rb the desolate|נְשַׁמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb cities.|וְעָרִ֥ים\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid,|תִּֽירְאִי֙\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be put to shame;|תֵב֔וֹשִׁי\rb*
\q2 \rb do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb be intimidated,|תִּכָּלְמִ֖י\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be humiliated.|תַחְפִּ֑ירִי\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you will forget|תִּשְׁכָּ֔חִי\rb* \rb the shame|בֹ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb of your youth|עֲלוּמַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and will remember|תִזְכְּרִי־\rb* \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb more|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb the reproach|וְחֶרְפַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of your widowhood.|אַלְמְנוּתַ֖יִךְ\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb your husband|בֹעֲלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb is your Maker—|עֹשַׂ֔יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֖וֹת\rb* \rb is His name—|שְׁמ֑וֹ\rb*
\q1 \rb the Holy|קְד֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb One of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb is your Redeemer;|וְגֹֽאֲלֵךְ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb He is called|יִקָּרֵֽא׃\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of all|כָל־\rb* \rb the earth.|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*
\q1 \v 6 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb has called you back,|קְרָאָ֣ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb like a wife|כְאִשָּׁ֧ה\rb* \rb deserted|עֲזוּבָ֛ה\rb* \rb and wounded|וַעֲצ֥וּבַת\rb* \rb in spirit,|ר֖וּחַ\rb*
\q1 \rb like|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the rejected|תִמָּאֵ֖ס\rb* \rb wife|וְאֵ֧שֶׁת\rb* \rb of one’s youth,”|נְעוּרִ֛ים\rb*
\q2 \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb your God.|אֱלֹהָֽיִךְ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb “For a brief|קָטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb moment|בְּרֶ֥גַע\rb* \rb I forsook you,|עֲזַבְתִּ֑יךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb but with great|גְּדֹלִ֖ים\rb* \rb compassion|וּבְרַחֲמִ֥ים\rb* \rb I will bring you back.|אֲקַבְּצֵֽךְ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 8 \rb In a surge|בְּשֶׁ֣צֶף\rb* \rb of anger|קֶ֗צֶף\rb*
\q2 \rb I hid|הִסְתַּ֨רְתִּי\rb* \rb My face|פָנַ֥י\rb* \rb from you|מִמֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb for a moment,|רֶ֙גַע֙\rb*
\q1 \rb but with everlasting|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb kindness|וּבְחֶ֥סֶד\rb* \rb I will have compassion on you,”|רִֽחַמְתִּ֑יךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb your Redeemer.|גֹּאֲלֵ֖ךְ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb “For|כִּי־\rb* \rb to Me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb this is like|זֹ֣את\rb*\rb |מֵ֥י\rb* \rb the days of Noah,|נֹ֙חַ֙\rb*\f + \fr 54:9 \ft Some manuscripts \fqa For this is like the waters of Noah\f*
\q2 \rb when|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I swore|נִשְׁבַּ֗עְתִּי\rb* \rb that the waters|מֵי־\rb* \rb of Noah|נֹ֛חַ\rb*
\q2 \rb would never again|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb cover|מֵעֲבֹ֥ר\rb* \rb the earth.|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q1 \rb So|כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb I have sworn|נִשְׁבַּ֛עְתִּי\rb* \rb that I will not be angry|מִקְּצֹ֥ף\rb* \rb with you|עָלַ֖יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb or rebuke|וּמִגְּעָר־\rb* \rb you.|בָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 10 \rb Though|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶֽהָרִים֙\rb* \rb may be removed|יָמ֔וּשׁוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the hills|וְהַגְּבָע֖וֹת\rb* \rb may be shaken,|תְּמוּטֶ֑נָה\rb*
\q1 \rb My loving devotion|וְחַסְדִּ֞י\rb*\rb |מֵאִתֵּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb depart from you,|יָמ֗וּשׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb and My covenant|וּבְרִ֤ית\rb* \rb of peace|שְׁלוֹמִי֙\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be broken,”|תָמ֔וּט\rb*
\q2 \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb who has compassion on you.|מְרַחֲמֵ֖ךְ\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb “O afflicted city,|עֲנִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb lashed by storms,|סֹעֲרָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb without|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb solace,|נֻחָ֑מָה\rb*
\q1 \rb surely|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֜י\rb* \rb will set|מַרְבִּ֤יץ\rb* \rb your stones|אֲבָנַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb in antimony|בַּפּוּךְ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and lay your foundations|וִיסַדְתִּ֖יךְ\rb* \rb with sapphires.|בַּסַּפִּירִֽים׃\rb*\f + \fr 54:11 \ft Or \fqa lapis lazuli\f*
\q1 \v 12 \rb I will make|וְשַׂמְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb your pinnacles|שִׁמְשֹׁתַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb of rubies,|כַּֽדְכֹד֙\rb*
\q2 \rb your gates|וּשְׁעָרַ֖יִךְ\rb* \rb of sparkling|אֶקְדָּ֑ח\rb* \rb jewels,|לְאַבְנֵ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your walls|גְּבוּלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb of precious|חֵֽפֶץ׃\rb* \rb stones.|לְאַבְנֵי־\rb*
\q1 \v 13 \rb Then all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your sons|בָּנַ֖יִךְ\rb* \rb will be taught|לִמּוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb by the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 54:13 \ft Cited in \ref John 6:45|JHN 6:45\ref*\f*
\q2 \rb and great|וְרַ֖ב\rb* \rb will be their|בָּנָֽיִךְ׃\rb* \rb prosperity.|שְׁל֥וֹם\rb*
\q1 \v 14 \rb In righteousness|בִּצְדָקָ֖ה\rb* \rb you will be established,|תִּכּוֹנָ֑נִי\rb*
\q2 \rb far|רַחֲקִ֤י\rb* \rb from oppression,|מֵעֹ֙שֶׁק֙\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you will have no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb fear.|תִירָ֔אִי\rb*
\q1 \rb Terror will be far removed,|וּמִ֨מְּחִתָּ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb come near|תִקְרַ֖ב\rb* \rb you.|אֵלָֽיִךְ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb If|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb anyone attacks you,|גּ֥וֹר\rb*\rb |יָג֛וּר\rb* \rb it is not|אֶ֖פֶס\rb* \rb from Me;|מֵֽאוֹתִ֑י\rb*
\q2 \rb whoever|מִי־\rb* \rb assails you|גָ֥ר\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb will fall|יִפּֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb before you.|עָלַ֥יִךְ\rb*
\q1 \v 16 \rb Behold,|הֵן\rb* \rb I|אָֽנֹכִי֙\rb* \rb have created|בָּרָ֣אתִי\rb* \rb the craftsman|חָרָ֔שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb who fans|נֹפֵ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb the coals|פֶּחָ֔ם\rb* \rb into flame|בְּאֵ֣שׁ\rb*
\q2 \rb and forges|וּמוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb a weapon|כְלִ֖י\rb* \rb fit for its task;|לְמַעֲשֵׂ֑הוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb and I|וְאָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb have created|בָּרָ֥אתִי\rb* \rb the destroyer|מַשְׁחִ֖ית\rb*
\q2 \rb to wreak havoc.|לְחַבֵּֽל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 17 \rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb No|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb weapon|כְּלִ֞י\rb* \rb formed|יוּצַ֤ר\rb* \rb against you|עָלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb shall prosper,|יִצְלָ֔ח\rb*
\q2 \rb and you will refute|תַּרְשִׁ֑יעִי\rb* \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb tongue|לָשׁ֛וֹן\rb* \rb that accuses|תָּֽקוּם־\rb*\rb |לַמִּשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb you.|אִתָּ֥ךְ\rb*
\q1 \rb This|זֹ֡את\rb* \rb is the heritage|נַחֲלַת֩\rb* \rb of the servants|עַבְדֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֧ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and their vindication|וְצִדְקָתָ֛ם\rb* \rb is from Me,”|מֵאִתִּ֖י\rb*
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*
\c 55
\s1 Invitation to the Needy
\q1 \v 1 \rb “Come,|ה֤וֹי\rb* \rb all you|כָּל־\rb* \rb who are thirsty,|צָמֵא֙\rb*
\q2 \rb come|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb to the waters;|לַמַּ֔יִם\rb*
\q1 \rb and you|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb without|אֵֽין־\rb*\rb |ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb money,|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*
\q2 \rb come,|לְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb buy,|שִׁבְרוּ֙\rb* \rb and eat!|וֶֽאֱכֹ֔לוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb Come,|וּלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb buy|שִׁבְר֗וּ\rb* \rb wine|יַ֥יִן\rb* \rb and milk|וְחָלָֽב׃\rb*
\q2 \rb without|בְּלוֹא־\rb* \rb money|כֶ֛סֶף\rb* \rb and without|וּבְל֥וֹא\rb* \rb cost!|מְחִ֖יר\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb Why|לָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb spend|תִשְׁקְלוּ־\rb* \rb money|כֶ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb on that which is not|בְּֽלוֹא־\rb* \rb bread,|לֶ֔חֶם\rb*
\q2 \rb and your labor|וִיגִיעֲכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb on that which does not|בְּל֣וֹא\rb* \rb satisfy?|לְשָׂבְעָ֑ה\rb*
\q1 \rb Listen carefully|שִׁמְע֨וּ\rb*\rb |שָׁמ֤וֹעַ\rb* \rb to Me,|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb and eat|וְאִכְלוּ־\rb* \rb what is good,|ט֔וֹב\rb*
\q2 \rb and your soul|נַפְשְׁכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb will delight|וְתִתְעַנַּ֥ג\rb* \rb in the richest of foods.|בַּדֶּ֖שֶׁן\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Incline|הַטּ֤וּ\rb* \rb your ear|אָזְנְכֶם֙\rb* \rb and come|וּלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb to Me;|אֵלַ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb listen,|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb so that your soul|נַפְשְׁכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb may live.|וּתְחִ֣י\rb*
\q1 \rb I will make|וְאֶכְרְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb with you|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb an everlasting|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb covenant—|בְּרִ֣ית\rb*
\q2 \rb My loving devotion|חַֽסְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb promised|הַנֶּאֱמָנִֽים׃\rb* \rb to David.|דָוִ֖ד\rb*\f + \fr 55:3 \ft Cited in \ref Acts 13:34|ACT 13:34\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 4 \rb Behold,|הֵ֛ן\rb* \rb I have made him|נְתַתִּ֑יו\rb* \rb a witness|עֵ֥ד\rb* \rb to the nations,|לְאוּמִּ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb a leader|נָגִ֥יד\rb* \rb and commander|וּמְצַוֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb of the peoples.|לְאֻמִּֽים׃\rb*
\q1 \v 5 \rb Surely|הֵ֣ן\rb* \rb you will summon|תִּקְרָ֔א\rb* \rb a nation|גּ֤וֹי\rb* \rb you do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb know,|תֵדַע֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and nations|וְג֥וֹי\rb* \rb who do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb know you|יְדָע֖וּךָ\rb* \rb will run|יָר֑וּצוּ\rb*\rb |לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb to you.|אֵלֶ֣יךָ\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb the Holy|וְלִקְד֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb One of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*
\q2 \rb has bestowed glory on you.”|פֵאֲרָֽךְ׃ס\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Seek|דִּרְשׁ֥וּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb while He may be found;|בְּהִמָּצְא֑וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb call on Him|קְרָאֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb while He is|בִּֽהְיוֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb near.|קָרֽוֹב׃\rb*
\q1 \v 7 \rb Let the wicked man|רָשָׁע֙\rb* \rb forsake|יַעֲזֹ֤ב\rb* \rb his way|דַּרְכּ֔וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the unrighteous|אָ֖וֶן\rb* \rb man|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb his thoughts;|מַחְשְׁבֹתָ֑יו\rb*
\q1 \rb let him return|וְיָשֹׁ֤ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb that He may have compassion,|וִֽירַחֲמֵ֔הוּ\rb*
\q1 \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb He will freely|יַרְבֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb pardon.|לִסְלֽוֹחַ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb “For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb My thoughts|מַחְשְׁבוֹתַי֙\rb* \rb are not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb your thoughts,|מַחְשְׁב֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb neither are|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb your ways|דַרְכֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb My ways,”|דְּרָכָ֑י\rb*
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb “For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb as the heavens|שָׁמַ֖יִם\rb* \rb are higher|גָבְה֥וּ\rb* \rb than the earth,|מֵאָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb My ways|דְרָכַי֙\rb* \rb are higher|גָּבְה֤וּ\rb* \rb than your ways|מִדַּרְכֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*
