\q2 \rb and I will make you ride|וְהִרְכַּבְתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the heights|בָּ֣מֳותֵי\rb* \rb of the land|אָ֑רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and feed you|וְהַאֲכַלְתִּ֗יךָ\rb* \rb with the heritage|נַחֲלַת֙\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Jacob.”|יַעֲקֹ֣ב\rb*
\qr \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the mouth|פִּ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has spoken.|דִּבֵּֽר׃ס\rb*
\c 59
\s1 Sin Separates Us from God
\r \ref Psalm 14:1–7|PSA 14:1-7\ref*; \ref Psalm 53:1–6|PSA 53:1-6\ref*; \ref Romans 3:9–20|ROM 3:9-20\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 \rb Surely|הֵ֛ן\rb* \rb the arm|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb too short|קָצְרָ֥ה\rb* \rb to save,|מֵֽהוֹשִׁ֑יעַ\rb*
\q2 \rb nor His ear|אָזְנ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb too dull|כָבְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb to hear.|מִשְּׁמֽוֹעַ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 2 \rb But|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb your iniquities|עֲוֺנֹֽתֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb have built barriers|מַבְדִּלִ֔ים\rb*
