\q1 \rb to bring|לְהָבִ֤יא\rb* \rb your children|בָנַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb from afar,|מֵֽרָח֔וֹק\rb*
\q2 \rb with|אִתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb their silver|כַּסְפָּ֥ם\rb* \rb and gold,|וּזְהָבָ֖ם\rb*
\q1 \rb to the honor|לְשֵׁם֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהַ֔יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb the Holy|וְלִקְד֥וֹשׁ\rb* \rb One of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb He has glorified you.|פֵאֲרָֽךְ׃\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Foreigners|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |נֵכָר֙\rb* \rb will rebuild|וּבָנ֤וּ\rb* \rb your walls,|חֹמֹתַ֔יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and their kings|וּמַלְכֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will serve you.|יְשָׁרְת֑וּנֶךְ\rb*
\q1 \rb Although|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I struck you|הִכִּיתִ֔יךְ\rb* \rb in anger,|בְקִצְפִּי֙\rb*
\q2 \rb yet in favor|וּבִרְצוֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb I will show you mercy.|רִֽחַמְתִּֽיךְ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 11 \rb Your gates|שְׁעָרַ֧יִךְ\rb* \rb will always|תָּמִ֛יד\rb* \rb stand open;|וּפִתְּח֨וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb they will never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be shut,|יִסָּגֵ֑רוּ\rb* \rb day|יוֹמָ֥ם\rb* \rb or night,|וָלַ֖יְלָה\rb*
\q1 \rb so that the wealth|חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb of the nations|גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb may be brought|לְהָבִ֤יא\rb* \rb into you,|אֵלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*
