\q2 \rb will no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb be heard|יִשָּׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb in her.|בָּהּ֙\rb*
\b 
\q1 \v 20 \rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb will a nursing infant|ע֤וּל\rb* \rb live|יִֽהְיֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֜ם\rb* \rb but a few days,|יָמִים֙\rb*
\q2 \rb or an old man|וְזָקֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb fail|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to live out|יְמַלֵּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his years.|יָמָ֑יו\rb*
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the youth|הַנַּ֗עַר\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֔וּת\rb* \rb at a hundred|מֵאָ֤ה\rb* \rb years,|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and he who fails|וְהַ֣חוֹטֶ֔א\rb* \rb to reach a hundred|מֵאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb will be considered accursed.|יְקֻלָּֽל׃\rb*
\q1 \v 21 \rb They will build|וּבָנ֥וּ\rb* \rb houses|בָתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb and dwell in them;|וְיָשָׁ֑בוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb they will plant|וְנָטְע֣וּ\rb* \rb vineyards|כְרָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and eat|וְאָכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb their fruit.|פִּרְיָֽם׃\rb*
\b 
